2 CONT
2 CONT ^ The date was argued for by J. S. P. Tatlock, "Caradoc of Llancarfan," Speculum 13, 144-45.
2 CONT
2 CONT ^ The New Statistical Account of Scotland, Perth, Vol. X, 1845, p. 1224; Doune Historical Notes, Forth Naturalist and Historian, Moray S. Mackay, Stirling, 1984, p. 72; Kilmadock in Dunblane Diocese, Society of Friends of Dunblane
2 CONC  Cathedral, Moray S. Mackay, Vol. XI. Part III, 1972, p. 83-85.
2 CONT
2 CONT ^ Discussed at length in Tatlock 1939.
2 CONT
2 CONT ^ usque ad tempus Hiuguel regis, filii Ouguenii regis Morganensium (quoted in Tatlock 1939:346.
2 CONT
2 CONT ^ "Certain innocent moderns, anxious to extract the uttermost farthing of historical truth from this yarn, have tried to identify 'Beneventana civitas' with some place in Britain," Tatlock observed and pointed out that the circula
2 CONC r Lombard church in Beneventum was dedicated to Saint Sophias, "a scarce name among saints. The inference is obvious that some Welsh visitor to Benevento had found there some name or anecdote to excuse the attractive invention tha
2 CONC t Cadoc had been there and was Sofia." (Tatlock 1939:346).
2 CONT
2 CONT ^ "Lives of the Cambro British saints",p. 378, 1853, Rev. William Jenkins Rees
