1 NOTE BIOGRAPHY: Cynwyd was the eldest of the three sons of Cunbelin ab Arthuis of the Pennines. It is unclear what portion of his grandfather's domain came Cynwyd's way: possibly the region around Caer-Lerion (Leicester). Was this area
2 CONC  named Cynwydion in his honour? Perhaps not. His son, King Cadrod, appears to have ruled further south.
2 CONT
2 CONT He supposedly married Peren daughter of Greidal ab Arthrwys ap Garmon and they had a disputed number of sons.
2 CONT
2 CONT  -- http://www.earlybritishkingdoms.com
