2 CONT ===The Lives of British Saints===
2 CONT '''Pg. 425''' – ELAETH, king, saint, and bard was the son of Meurig ab Idno of the raxe of Coel Hen, by Onen Greg (“Ash-tree the Hoarse”), daughter of '''Gwallog ab Lleenog''', one of the three “Battle-pillars of Britain”.[1] '''G
2 CONC wallog is sometimes also given as father of Dwywai, wife of Duawd.'''
2 CONT
2 CONT [1] Peniarth MSS. 16 and 45; Hafod MS. 16; Cambro-British Saints, pp. 266, 269; Myv. Arch., p. 424; Iolo MSS., pp 103, 112, 134)   [https://www.google.com/books/edition/The_Lives_of_the_British_Saints/-G4AAAAAMAAJ?hl=en&gbpv=1&bsq
2 CONC =Dwywai]
