2 CONT Page 43:
2 CONT
2 CONT 7. Donald I Brecc (Domnall the Speckled), d. Dec. 642?  King of Dalriada from 629; a promoter of Christianity; killed at the Battle of Strathcairn, Ross-shire.  There is reason to believe that the Caledonian kings held some power 
2 CONC over the old Irish homeland until this time.
2 CONT
2 CONT !Availability: The libraries of Ken, Karen, Kristen, Kevin, Brian, Amie, Adam and FAL.
2 CONT
2 CONT Source: "Ancestral Roots of Sixty Colonists" by Frederick Lewis Weis.
2 CONT
2 CONT Page 144 line (170-7):
2 CONT
2 CONT 7.  Domnall Brecc, killed at the battle of Strathcarron, prob. about 642 A.D.  He is apparently the last king of Dalriada known to early Welsh tradition.
1 NOTE From Genealogical Library book "House of Adam".
1 NOTE From Genealogical Library book "House of Adam".
1 NOTE Domnall Brecc 
2 CONT http://trees.ancestry.com/rd?f=document&guid=07497838-b986-40c8-b699-ccd999ffe959&tid=7053141&pid=-1136462591
1 NOTE Pedigrees prior to the sixth century are based upon potentially conflicting oral traditions.
1 NOTE OR "DOMNALL"; KNOWN AS "THE SPECKLED"; KING OF DAL RIADA 636-650
1 NOTE He ruled from 629 to 642. According ot Welsh tratdition, he is the last King of Dalriada known. He died in battle.
1 NOTE King of Scots of Argyll, perhaps maternally King of the Picts d c 629
1 NOTE He ruled from 629 to 642. According ot Welsh tratdition, he is the last King of Dalriada known. He died in battle.
1 NOTE Killed in battle about 643.[FAVthomas.FTW]
2 CONT
2 CONT    Domnall Brecc succeeded to the kingship in 629, when his predecessor,Connad Cerr,was killed in Ireland after a three month reign. Domnall waseither incompetent, unlucky or both; he never won a battle. His firstdefeat came in 63
2 CONC 5 in a battle which was possibly against the Picts. In637 he was defeated at the battle of Mag Rath in Ireland, and from thispoint on the kings of Dal Riata completely lost control of their Irishpossessions. It was probably about 
2 CONC this point that Domnall was demoted tothe position of joint king with his third cousin Ferchar, son of ConnadCerr. Domnall was defeated yet again,
2 CONT possibly by the Picts, in 638. He finally met his death in 642, at thehands of the Britons of Strathclyde. He was succeeded by his joint kingFerchar.
1 NOTE 1  UID 094D5BDBF7694A45A7E16BF6E6B36D64CE32
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT 630-634 C.E.
