1 NAME Manwgan, King of Powys
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE ABT 610
2 PLAC Powys, Wales
2 ADDR
1 OCCU King of Powys, King of Powis (r.613....642-~655)
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} See Peter Bartrum, https://www.geni.com/documents/view?doc_id=6000000173392952886 (February 6, 2023; Anne Brannen, curator)
2 CONT
2 CONT Manwgan ap Selyf was an early 7th century King of Powys, the son of Selyf Sarffgadau.
2 CONT
2 CONT One theory asserts that when Manwgan ap Selyf came to the throne in 613 he was a young boy, which led to an invasion of Powys by Eluadd ap Glast (alias Eiludd Powys), the erstwhile King of Dogfeiling. The usurper probably managed 
2 CONC to hold the throne for some thirty years or more before he was killed fighting the Northumbrians, possibly at the Battle of Maes Cogwy (Oswestry) in 642. The Dogfeiling dynasty was finally crushed by the Saxons around 656, and Man
2 CONC wgan was able to take his rightful place on the Powysian throne.
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Also called Mancenn English. Also called Manucanus Latin. Brenin Powys Manwgan ap Selyfan o Powys was born circa 610.1 He was the successor of Brenin Powys Selyf Sarffgadau ap Cynan o Powys; King of Powys.2 Brenin Powys Manwgan ap
2 CONC  Selyfan o Powys was the son of Brenin Powys Selyf Sarffgadau ap Cynan o Powys.1 Brenin Powys Manwgan ap Selyfan o Powys was appears to have been a very small boy when his father, Selyf Sarffgadau (Battle-Snake) was killed at the 
2 CONC Battle of Caer-Legion (Chester) in 613.1 One theory asserts that this, the death of Selyd, led to an invasion of Powys by Eluadd ap Glast (alias Eluan Powys), the erstwhile King of Dogfeiling. The usurper probably managed to hold 
2 CONC the throne for some thirty years or more before he was killed fighting the Northumbrians, possibly at the Battle of Maes-Cogwy (Oswestry) in 642. The Dogfeiling dynasty was finally crushed by the Saxons around 656, and Manwgan was
2 CONC  able to take his rightful place on the Powysian throne. After 613. King of Powys at Wales in 642?.2 He was the predecessor of Brenin Powys Beli ab Eiludd o Powys; King of Powys.2
2 CONT
2 CONT Family
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Child	
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Brenin Powys Beli ab Eiludd o Powys+ b. c 6351
2 CONT
2 CONT http://homepages.rootsweb.ancestry.com/~cousin/html/p94.htm#i11700
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT One theory asserts that when Manwgan ap Selyf came to the throne in 613 he was a young boy, which led to an invasion of Powys by Eluadd ap Glast (alias Eiludd Powys), the erstwhile King of Dogfeiling. The usurper probably managed 
2 CONC to hold the throne for some thirty years or more before he was killed fighting the Northumbrians, possibly at the Battle of Maes Cogwy (Oswestry) in 642. The Dogfeiling dynasty was finally crushed by the Saxons around 656.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Usurped by Eiludd (Elfan)(ap Cyndrwyn), King of Dogfeiling in 613 (not related) as an infant. Restored about 642 after Eiludd was killed fighting the Northumbrians. Many chronologies falsely assume this Eiludd was Beli's father.
