1 NOTE [De La Pole.FTW]
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources: Kraentzler 1748, 1749; History of Morgan Family.
2 CONT    History: King of Gwynned 625. Died 633-634.   Cadwallon engaged in a series of ferocious battles with the Saxons. He married the daughter of Pebba, the King of Mercia, and was killed in battle with Oswald, King of Northumbria. 
2 CONC His son was Cadwaladr.
2 CONT    K: Cadwallon, King of Brittain. Died 659.
2 CONT    AF calls him King of North Wales.                            ******* Cadwallon was the King of the Britons and, as an ally of King of Penda of Mercia, defeated Edwin of Northumbria in 633. [Sources 2 and 3]
2 CONT King of Gwynedd, 625.  Cadwallon engaged in a series of ferocious battles with the Saxons.  He married the daughter of Pebba, the King of Mercia, and was killed in battle with Oswald, King of Northumbria.  His son was Cadwaladr. [
2 CONC Source 1]
2 CONT
2 CONT SOURCES:
2 CONT   1.  Morgan, Dennis.  _A History of the Morgan Family_.  2.  The American Genealogist (TAG), Vol. 41, No. 4, Oct. 1965, "The Paternal
2 CONT       Ancestry of Rhodri Mawr".  3.  The American Genealogist (TAG), Vol. 41, No. 1, Jan. 1965, "The House of
2 CONT       Cunedda".
