2 CONT
2 CONT Beli ap Eiludd was a 7th century King of Powys.
2 CONT
2 CONT Some theories assert that he was in fact the son of Manwgan ap Selyf who regained power after Eiludd Powys was killed at the battle of Battle of Maes Cogwy in 642.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Beli ap Eilud===
2 CONT '''Born''' about 0610
2 CONT '''Father''': Eilud ap Cynan, born about 0590
2 CONT '''Mother''': unknown
2 CONT '''Siblings''': unknown
2 CONT '''Spouse''': unknown
2 CONT '''Child''': Gwylog ap Beli King of Powys, born about 0640
2 CONT '''Source''': ancestry.com
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Brenin Powys Beli ab Eiludd o Powys was probably not related to Eiludd, who was from a rival House.2 He was born circa 635.1 He was the son of Brenin Powys Manwgan ap Selyfan o Powys.1 Brenin Powys Beli ab Eiludd o Powys was the s
2 CONC uccessor of Brenin Powys Manwgan ap Selyfan o Powys; King of Powys.2 King of Powys at Wales circa 655.2 Brenin Powys Beli ab Eiludd o Powys was the predecessor of Brenin Powys Gwylog ap Beli o Powys; King of Powys.2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Family'''
2 CONT '''Child''': 	Brenin Powys Gwylog ap Beli o Powys+ b. c 6601
