1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eochaid_mac_Domangairt
2 CONT
2 CONT Notes for Eochaidh II Of Argyll King Of Dal Riata 
2 CONT
2 CONT Weis' "Ancestral Roots. . ." (170:9). 
2 CONT
2 CONT the following is taken from an Internet posting of Michael R. Davidson of Edinburgh. Scotland, on 23 Oct 1995: 
2 CONT
2 CONT Eochaid mac Domangart 
2 CONT
2 CONT Eochaid succeeded to a kingship in turmoil in 697. In 695, Domnall Donn, the king of Dal Riata and Eochaid's father's cousin was killed by the Cenel Loairn, a rival branch of the Dal Riata. The Cenel Loairn claimant, Ferchar Fota,
2 CONC  was then recognized as king of Dal Riata. When Ferchar died in 697, Eochaid briefly held the kingship, until he was, in turn, killed by the Cenel Loairn. Ferchar's son Ainbcellach succeeded in the kingship. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Children: 
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. *Eochaid. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 2. Alpin, probably expelled from the kingship of Dal Riata by Oengus, king of the Picts in 736. 
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.southing.net/BondFam019%20Web%20Cards/PS02/PS02_125.HTM
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Eochaid_II .  Died 700.  !GENEALOGY: Royal Ancestors of Magna
2 CONT
2 CONT          Charta Barons; Page; 226; G929.72; C6943ra; Denver Public
2 CONT
2 CONT          Library; Genealogy
2 CONT
2 CONT               Children of Eochaid_II  and _____:
2 CONT
2 CONT              9       i   Eochaid_III (Eugenius)
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Eochaid Riannamail "Crook-nose" mac Domangart
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Eochaid mac Domangairt''' (died ca. 697) was a king of Dál Riata (modern western Scotland) in about 697. He was a member of the Cenél nGabráin, the son of Domangart mac Domnaill and father of Eochaid mac Echdach; Alpín mac Echd
2 CONC ach may also be a son of this Eochaid.
2 CONT
2 CONT He is named in Dál Riata king-lists, the Duan Albanach and the ''Synchronisms'' of Flann Mainistrech. In some sources he is called Eochaid Crook-Nose (''Riannamail''), but modern readings take this is a being a garbled reference t
2 CONC o Fiannamail ua Dúnchado rather than an epithet.
2 CONT
2 CONT The killing of ''Eochu nepos Domnaill'', Eochaid grandson of Domnall Brecc, is reported in the ''Annals of Ulster'' for 697.
2 CONT
2 CONT ==References==
2 CONT * Alan Orr Anderson|Anderson, Alan Orr, ''Early Sources of Scottish History A.D 500&ndash;1286'', volume 1. Reprinted with corrections. Paul Watkins, Stamford, 1990. ISBN 1-871615-03-8
2 CONT * Dauvit Broun|Broun, Dauvit, ''The Irish Identity of the Kingdom of the Scots in the Twelfth and Thirteenth Centuries.'' Boydell, Woodbridge, 1999. ISBN 0-85115-375-5
2 CONT
2 CONT ==External links==
2 CONT *[http://celt.ucc.ie/index.html CELT: Corpus of Electronic Texts] at [http://www.ucc.ie/ University College Cork] includes the ''Annals of Ulster'', ''Tigernach'', ''the Four Masters'' and ''Innisfallen'', the ''Chronicon Scotorum
2 CONC '', the ''Lebor Bretnach'' (which includes the ''Duan Albanach''), Genealogies, and various Saints' Lives. Most are translated into English, or translations are in progress.
2 CONT
