2 CONT Page 44:
2 CONT
2 CONT 12.  Eochy IV  Annuine (Eochaid the Poisonous), d. 834; King of Delriada from 781; possibly mar. the only dau. of Wroid, King of Picts 775-79.  All these Eochys, a favorite Irish name, were so called after Eochy Munrevar, father o
2 CONC f Ercc.
2 CONT
2 CONT !Availability: The libraries of Ken, Karen, Kristen, Kevin, Brian, Amie, Adam and FAL
2 CONT
2 CONT Source: "Ancestral Roots of Sixty Colonists" by Frederick Lewis Weis.
2 CONT
2 CONT Page 144 line (170-11):
2 CONT
2 CONT 11.  Eochaid. The Poisonous, King of Dalriada, 781 ff.
1 NOTE Killed in 697. King of Dalriada.
1 NOTE BIOGRAPHY
2 CONT The ancestry of Eochaid goes back to Fergus 'the Great', King of Scots of Dalriada, straddling the Irish Channel from Antrim to Argyll who was killed in 501. However the lineage is somewhat confused and uncertain. About 780 Eochai
2 CONC d, 'the Venomous' or 'the Poisonous', became King of Scots of Argyll. He married his cousin Fergusa whose mother was a Pictish princess.
