1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''HYWEL ap RHODRI MOLWYNOG'''  From http://wbo.llgc.org.uk/en/s-HYWE-RHO-0825.html
2 CONT
2 CONT (d. 825 ), king of Gwynedd ; a great-grandson of Cadwaladr (d. 664 ) (q.v.) , and the last king in Anglesey of the line of Cunedda (q.v.) . The blood of Cunedda was transmitted, on Hywel 's death, to a new royal house through his 
2 CONC niece, Ethyllt (grandmother of Rhodri the Great ) (q.v. ), daughter of his brother, Cynan (d. 816 ), with whom he had for long contested Anglesey . 
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Bibliography:==
2 CONT ■A History of Wales  Author: Professor Thomas Jones Pierce, M.A., F.S.A., (1905-1964), Aberystwyth. 
2 CONT
2 CONT
