2 CONT Also called King Rhain of Brycheiniog. Brenin Ddyfed a Brycheiniog Rhain I ap Cadwgn Trydelig o Ddyfed was related to Brenin Brycheiniog Tewdr ap Rhein o Ddyfed; the second son of Rhein, and brother of Tewdos, King of Dyfed.3 Bren
2 CONC in Ddyfed a Brycheiniog Rhain I ap Cadwgn Trydelig o Ddyfed was born circa 690.2 He was the predecessor of Brenin Ddyfed a Brycheiniog Cadwgn Trydelig ap Cathen o Ddyfed; King of Dyfed and Brycheiniog.3 Brenin Ddyfed a Brycheiniog
2 CONC  Rhain I ap Cadwgn Trydelig o Ddyfed was the son of Brenin Ddyfed a Brycheiniog Cadwgn Trydelig ap Cathen o Ddyfed.2,1 Brenin Ddyfed a Brycheiniog Rhain I ap Cadwgn Trydelig o Ddyfed was living in 710.4 King of Dyfed at South Wale
2 CONC s after 710. King of Brycheiniog at the Brecon Beacons, Powys, Wales, circa 715.3 He was the predecessor of Brenin Brycheiniog Awst ap Cadwgn Trydelig o Ddyfed; King of Brycheiniog.3 Brenin Ddyfed a Brycheiniog Rhain I ap Cadwgn T
2 CONC rydelig o Ddyfed was the successor of Brenin Ddyfed Tewdos ap Rhein o Ddyfed; King of Dyfed.3 Brenin Ddyfed a Brycheiniog Rhain I ap Cadwgn Trydelig o Ddyfed saw his county invaded by Seisyll of Ceredigion, his 7th cousin 1x remov
2 CONC ed, circa 740.2
