2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Cynan Dindaethwy ap Rhodri (English: Cynan of Dindaethwy, son of Rhodri) was King of Gwynedd (reigned 798 – 816). His reign was marked by a destructive dynastic power struggle with his brother Hywel, and is not otherwise notable.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Cynan Dindaethwy ap Rhodri, also known as Cynan Dindaethwy, was King of Gwynedd in medieval northwest Wales, also called King of the Britons by the Annals of Ulster.
2 CONT
2 CONT Cynan ascended to the throne of Gwynedd after first his father died and then his cousin Caradog ap Meirion, who had become king after Rhodri, died in 798.
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Cynan Dindaethwy ap Rhodri
2 CONT
2 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
2 CONT
2 CONT Cynan Dindaethwy ap Rhodri - Cynan Dindaethwy - was King of Gwynedd (798 – 816) in medieval north-west Wales, referred to as "King of the Britons" by the Annals of Ulster.
2 CONT
2 CONT Cynan was son of Rhodri Molwynog ap Idwal and Margaret ferch Duplory and ascended to the throne of Gwynedd after first his father died and then his cousin Caradog ap Meirion, who had become king after Rhodri, died in 798.
2 CONT
2 CONT Cynan Dindaethwy ap Rhodri was preceded by Caradog ap Meirion (c. 754-c. 798) and was succeeded by Hywel ap Rhodri Molwynog (814-825).
2 CONT
2 CONT Cynan Dindaethwy ap Rhodri Molwynog, Brenin Gwynedd1,2,3
