2 CONT
2 CONT -------------------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Came from the realm of Powys.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources:<br/>
2 CONT The book, 'Kings & Queens of Great Britain'<br/>
2 CONT The book, The Oxford History of the British Monarchy'
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Queen of Wales
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT The view that Ethyllt was Merfyn's mother and Nest his wife is held by Davies[9] and many others, including David E. Thornton[7] and Lloyd,[10] who notes the consistency of the genealogies in Jesus College MS 20 and Harleian MS 38
2 CONC 59 against the contrary account that Nest was the mother and Ethyllt the wife.
2 CONT
2 CONT The earliest writers of the history of Wales, from Dr David Powell in 1584 to Jane Williams in 1869, adopted the view of ABT that Nest was the mother of Merfyn Frych.  Although she is wholly absent from the Harleian Ms 3859 pedigr
2 CONC ees, that manuscript did name the mother of Merfyn Frych as "Etthil merch Cinnan".
2 CONT
2 CONT Around the final half of the 14th century, a group of pedigrees were set down in Jesus College Ms 20. This is the earliest appearance of a "Nest ferch Cadell m. Brochuael m. Elisse" and she is made the mother of Rhodri Mawr (thus 
2 CONC the wife of Merfyn Frych).  A number of years later, about 1400, the manuscripts now called Achau Brenhinoedd a Thywysogion Cymru (often abbreviated as ABT) set down the pedigrees of the dynastic kings and princes of Wales.  Here,
2 CONC  "Nest ferch Gadell ap Brochwal ap Elisse" is cited as the mother of Merfyn Frych (thus the wife of Gwriad ap Elidyr).  One might reasonably assume the objective of those medieval genealogists was to introduce a Powys heiress thro
2 CONC ugh whom the kingdom of Powys had been inherited by Gwynedd's Merfyn Frych or Rhodri Mawr, and it didn't really matter which. 
2 CONT
2 CONT The genealogies themselves are contained in a number of medieval manuscripts, the most important of which are detailed below.
2 CONT
2 CONT A: The Harleian genealogies
2 CONT
2 CONT Which are the earliest surviving document preserved in a single manuscript Harleian MS 3859, bound together with what is known as the 'A' version of the Annales Cambriae. The manuscript itself dates from around 1100, but as the ge
2 CONC nealogies begin with Owain ap Hywel Dda it is generally presumed that they were originally compiled during his reign (that is between 950 and 987) but are obviously based on oral recollections of a much older date.
2 CONT
2 CONT B: The Jesus College genealogies
2 CONT
2 CONT These are contained in the Jesus College MS 20, folios 33r to 41r and draws on the same body of material, but also contains some variations and additions which suggests that it was not directly derived from the Harleian MS. Howeve
2 CONC r, the Jesus College manuscript is dated to the late fourteenth century but was probably compiled in the thirteenth century. It is therefore of a much later date than the Harleian genealogies and is therefore considered to be less
2 CONC  reliable.
2 CONT
2 CONT The birthdate of Esyllt verch Cynan is often given as "c. 770", even when she is shown as mother of Merfyn, born "c. 764", as seen below. There is no documentation for either date.
2 CONT
2 CONT Esyllt verch Cynan   
2 CONT
2 CONT Esyllt was born about 0770 in Caer Seiont, Carnarvonshire, Wales.1   Esyllt's father was Cynan (Dindaethwy) ap Rhodri and her mother was <Unknown>.  Her paternal grandparents were Rhodri (Molwynog) ap Idwal and <Unknown>.  She was
2 CONC  an only child.
2 CONT
2 CONT spouse: <br/>
2 CONT Gwriad ap Elidir
2 CONT
2 CONT Gwriad was born about 0738 in Wales.1 
2 CONT
2 CONT Children<br/>
2 CONT Merfyn (The Freckled) Frych ap Gwriad
2 CONT
2 CONT Merfyn, known as The Freckled, was born in 0764 in Wales.2   He died as a war casualty at the age of 80 in 0844 in Battle of Cyfeil, Ketell, Wales.2 
2 CONT
2 CONT Cadrod ap Gwriad<br/>
2 CONT Cadrod was born about 0768.3 
2 CONT
2 CONT Esyllt ferch Cynan Dindaethwy1,2,3,4<br/>
2 CONT b. circa 770
2 CONT
2 CONT Father	Cynan Dindaethwy ap Rhodri Molwynog, Brenin Gwynedd1,5,2,3 b. circa 720?, d. 816
2 CONT
2 CONT Mother	Matilda of Flint1 b. circa 720
2 CONT
2 CONT      Esyllt ferch Cynan Dindaethwy married Gwriad ab Elidyr, Brenin Ynys Manau, son of Elidyr ap Sandde, Brenin Ynys Manau and Celemion verch Tudwal o Ynys Manau, before 764.2 Esyllt ferch Cynan Dindaethwy was born circa 770 at Ca
2 CONC er Seiont, Caernarvonshire, Wales.6 She was the daughter of Cynan Dindaethwy ap Rhodri Molwynog, Brenin Gwynedd and Matilda of Flint.1,5,2,3
2 CONT
2 CONT Family
2 CONT
2 CONT Gwriad ab Elidyr, Brenin Ynys Manau b. circa 750, d. 825
2 CONT
2 CONT Child	
2 CONT
2 CONT Brenin Gwynedd Merfyn Frych ap Gwriad o ne Rheged+ b. c 764, d. 8446,3
2 CONT
