2 CONT Bartrum originally charted her as a wife of Rhys ap Ithel ap Morgan ap Athrwys, but a look at that chart as emended by Bartrum shows that he realized that was chronologically impossible. JC 20,12 lists Ceingar as the mother of  Ar
2 CONC thfael, the second great grandfather of Morgan ap Owain. As such, Arthfael would date c. 765, making Ceingar c. 750. As such she would fit as a daughter for a c. 715 Maredudd ap Tuedos, and wife of c. 730 Brochwel ap Meurig ap Art
2 CONC hfael ap Rhys ap Ithel ap Morgan ap Athrwys. (Steven Ferry, April 19, 2021.)
