2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Cadell ap Rhodri (854–909) was King of Seisyllwg, a minor kingdom in southwestern Wales, from about 872 until his death.
2 CONT
2 CONT Cadell was the second son of Rhodri the Great of Gwynedd and Angharad, a princess from Seisyllwg. In 872 Angharad's brother Gwgon, King of Seisyllwg, drowned without leaving an heir. Rhodri became steward over the kingdom, and whi
2 CONC le he was unable to make a legal claim to the throne, he was able to install Cadell as king.[1] He passed it to his son, Hywel Dda, at his death in 909. Cadell and Hywel together also conquered Dyfed in 904–905, establishing Hywel
2 CONC  as the king in that region. After his father's death, Hywel ruled the kingdoms jointly as Deheubarth.
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT The wife of Cadell is unknown.  (See http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/WALES.htm)
