1 NOTE {geni:about_me} See Peter Bartrum, https://cadair.aber.ac.uk/dspace/bitstream/handle/2160/6516/TABLES%20-%20EARLY%20SERIES_42.png?sequence=13&isAllowed=y (May 27, 2018; Anne Brannen, curator)
2 CONT
2 CONT Darrell Wolcott shows that Merfyn ap Rhodri Mawr had no sons other than Triffyn ( he proposes that this man was actually a son-in-law of Rhodri ap Merfyn, Llewelyn ap Pasgen ap Urien known as Llewelyn Llyminiog Angel :
2 CONT
2 CONT Please see Darrell Wolcott: The Royal Family of Powys - Powys Succession after 823; http://www.ancientwalesstudies.org/id13.html. (Steven Ferry, October 15, 2019.)
2 CONT
2 CONT Please see Darrell Wolcott: Edwin of Tegeingl and His Family - Was Owain ap Edwin Really a Traitor; http://www.ancientwalesstudies.org/id87.html. (Steven Ferry, June 8, 2020.)
2 CONT
2 CONT Please see Darrell Wolcott: The Men of Lleyn - How They Got There; http://www.ancientwalesstudies.org/id118.html. (Steven Ferry, August 17, 2020.)
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Llewelyn was excluded from his crown by his uncle Cadell, and his cousin, Hywel Dha, who later married his daughter, Angharad.
2 CONT
2 CONT From: http://www.robertsewell.ca/powys.html
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Excluded from his throne by the usurpation of his uncle Cadell, and his cousin Howel Dha, successively Kings of South Wales.
2 CONT
