2 CONT Elen ferch Llywarch o Ddyfed
2 CONT
2 CONT b. circa 893, d. 929
2 CONT
2 CONT Father	Brenin Ddyfed Llywarch ap Hyfaidd o Ddyfed1,2 b. circa 840, d. 904
2 CONT
2 CONT      Elen ferch Llywarch o Ddyfed was born circa 893 at Dyfed, Wales.3,4 She was the daughter of Brenin Ddyfed Llywarch ap Hyfaidd o Ddyfed.1,2 Elen ferch Llywarch o Ddyfed married Hywel Dda ap Cadell, Brenin Cymru, son of Brenin 
2 CONC Seisyllwg Cadell ap Rhodri o Gwynedd and Rheingar (?), in 904.5,6 Elen ferch Llywarch o Ddyfed died in 929. "Helena obiit."1,7
2 CONT
2 CONT Family
2 CONT
2 CONT Hywel Dda ap Cadell, Brenin Cymru b. 887, d. 950
2 CONT
2 CONT Children	
2 CONT
2 CONT Angharad verch Hywel+ b. c 9108
2 CONT
2 CONT Brenin Deheubarth Owain ap Hywel Dda+ b. 913, d. 9881,9
2 CONT
2 CONT Rhodri ap Hywel b. c 920, d. c 953
2 CONT
2 CONT Edwin ap Hywel b. c 922, d. c 954
2 CONT
2 CONT Citations
2 CONT
2 CONT [S483] Stewart Baldwin, Llywelyn ap Iorwerth's ancestors in "Baldwin-Llywelyn," listserve message Dec 1998.
2 CONT
2 CONT [S492] Genealogies from Harleian MS. 3859, manuscript, probably between 954 and 988 unknown repository, 2: "Elen merc Ioumarc" (a mistake for "Loumarc").
2 CONT
2 CONT [S245] LDS.
2 CONT
2 CONT [S278] DfAdam, online unknown url, The Line of Eochaid Allmuir mac Airt Cuirp, 118.
2 CONT
2 CONT [S899] Castles of Wales, online http://www.castlewales.com/home.html#Please Select.
2 CONT
2 CONT [S640] History Files, online http://homepages.tesco.net/~plk33/plk33/history.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT [S485] Various, Annales Cambriae, "B" MS. of AC (BL MS. Cotton Domitian A.1) .
2 CONT
2 CONT [S278] DfAdam, online unknown url, The Line of Cadell ap Rhodri, King of Seisyllwg, 86.
2 CONT
2 CONT [S492] Genealogies from Harleian MS. 3859, manuscript, probably between 954 and 988 unknown repository, 2 - appears as "[O]uein map Elen" which gives his ancestry through his mother..
2 CONT
2 CONT Contemporary records show that he married ELEN, daughter of LLYWARCH ap HYFAIDD, the last of the royal line of Dyfed, who had died in 904. Her line is one of our earliest, being known back for five generations to II.398,589,988.MA
2 CONC REDUDD ap TEWDWS (d. 796), and this Dyfed line descended from members of an Irish tribe, the Déisi who migrated to Wales in the 4th century (Maund pp.23-24). 
2 CONT
2 CONT Hywel (The Good) ap Cadell & Elen verch Llywarch 
2 CONT
2 CONT They had eight sons and two daughters, named Owain, Maredydd, Rhodri, Rhain, Dyfnwal, Edwin, Cynan, Einion, Angharad and Gwenllian.
2 CONT
2 CONT Personal Details
2 CONT
2 CONT  Hywel (The Good) ap Cadell
2 CONT
2 CONT Hywel, known as The Good, was born about 0880.1   He died in 0950.1 
2 CONT
2 CONT  Elen verch Llywarch
2 CONT
2 CONT Elen was born about 0893 in Dynevor, Llandyfeisant, Carmarthenshire, Wales.1   She died in 0943.1 
2 CONT
