3 TITL Hywel ap Gronwy o Deheubarth - AncientWalesStudies.org
3 NOTE These should *always* be lowercase.
4 CONT Ap, ab, map = 'son of' (Welsh)
4 CONT verch, ferch = 'daughter of' (Welsh)
4 CONT ni, ingen = 'daughter of' (Irish Gaelic)
4 CONT mac = 'son of' (Irish Gaelic)
4 CONT ui = 'from the family of' (Irish Gaelic)
4 CONT o = 'of' (Welsh and Irish Gaelic)
3 NOTE "ap" usually means "son of", or the equivalent. For girls there is "ferch" or "verch", or some variation of these.
3 NOTE Just looking for Gruffud Ap Einion, I don't know what the Ap means in the names, I've run across it numerous times.    Tim Day
