1 NOTE The only daughter and heiress of Maredudd ab Owain, King of Deheubarth and Gwynedd, who was married while still a child to Llywelyn ap Seisyll, who succeeded his father-in-law and made himself ruler or overlord of all Wales.  He d
2 CONC ied in 1023 and was succeeded by his and Angharad's only son, Gruffydd ap Llywelyn.  Angharad, who must have been in her late thirties, then married Cynfyn ap Gwerstan, 'a noble of Powys', and had two more sons, Bleddyn ap Cynfyn 
2 CONC and Rhiwallon. [Cope.FTW]
