1 NOTE {geni:about_me} See Peter Bartrum, https://cadair.aber.ac.uk/dspace/bitstream/handle/2160/6516/TABLES%20-%20EARLY%20SERIES_42.png?sequence=13&isAllowed=y (May 27, 2018; Anne Brannen, curator)
2 CONT
2 CONT Please see Darrell Wolcott: Edwin of Tegeingl and His Family - The Ancestry of Edwin of Tegeingl; http://www.ancientwalesstudies.org/id42.html. "The majority, but by no means all, of the medieval pedigrees name the father of Edwin
2 CONC  as Gronwy.[3]  And say this Gronwy was the son of Owain ap Hywel Dda.  But since such a Gronwy would occur c. 940/950, he would be a full generation too old to be the father of Edwin.  Revised pedigrees were soon circulated which
2 CONC  "corrected" this to Gronwy ap Einion ap Owain ap Hywel Dda.  But none of the ancient manuscripts included a son of Einion ap Owain who was named Gronwy.  There was, however, an Edwin ap Einion born c. 980 and the occurrance of th
2 CONC at male name in the family of Owain ap Hywel Dda is likely the main reason why the medieval genealogists attached the later Edwin of Tegeingl to this line." (Steven Ferry, June 5, 2020.)
2 CONT
2 CONT Please see Darrell Wolcott: Maredudd ap Owain, King of Deheubarth; http://www.ancientwalesstudies.org/id206.html. (Steven Ferry, July 17, 2020.)
2 CONT
