2 CONT Family Links Spouses/Children: 1. Haer FERCH CYNILLIN Maredudd AP BLEDDYN+ Cadwgon AP BLEDDYN of Nannau, King of Powys+ Gwenllian FERCH BLEDDYN 2. Miss FERCH BROCHWEL Efa FERCH BLEDDYN+ Hunydd FERCH BLEDDYN Bleddyn "Sais" AP CYNFY
2 CONC N Prince of Powys 4850,8457
2 CONT
2 CONT Born: Abt 1025, Powys, Montgomeryshire, Wales Married (1): 1044 Married (2): Before 1058, 2nd wife Died: 1075
2 CONT
2 CONT    Another name for Bleddyn was Bleddyn ÀP MORIEN.
2 CONT
2 CONT    General Notes:
2 CONT
2 CONT All of the following information came from Jane Williams Flank, World Connect db=jwflank, rootsweb.com:
2 CONT
2 CONT Bleddyn Cynfyn ruled Powys 1063-1075
2 CONT
2 CONT _____________________ From http://homepages.tesco.net/~plk33/plk33/History/KingListBritain:
2 CONT
2 CONT By 1063, Blethyn (Bleddyn) rules a mostly united Wales, and Powys is detached from Gwynedd & Deheubarth for, or by, his son.
2 CONT
2 CONT _____________________
2 CONT
2 CONT Bleddyn and his brother Rhiwallon were half-brothers of Gruffydd ap Llywelyn. Their mother, Angharad, married Cynfyn ap Gwerstan o the death of Llywelyn ap Seisyll. Cynfyn ap Bwerstan may have been a Powys nobleman; there is also 
2 CONC some suggestion that he may have been half Saxon. Bleddyn remained a strong supporter of the Mercians in their battles against the Normans.
2 CONT
2 CONT Bleddyn and Rhiwallon also had to contend with internal revolution. The sons of Gruffydd ap Llywelyn, Maredudd and Idwal, attempted to reestablish their claim to the throne. However, they were also killed in the Battle of Mechain 
2 CONC in 1070; Bleddyn now ruled without internal challenge.
2 CONT
2 CONT He is reported to having been a generous king, giving to church and populous. He was the first king in over 100 years to revise the laws developed under Hywel Dda.
2 CONT
2 CONT Unfortunately, in 1073, the Normans began their advance through north Wales, and defeated Bleddyn in a surprise attack. Weakened, he became vurnerable to his southern neighbor, Rhys ab Owain of Deheubarth. In 1075, Rhys betrayed B
2 CONC leddyn, leading to his murder. However, Bleddyn's descendents became the main ruling family of Powys. [The Welsh Kings]
2 CONT
2 CONT _______________________
2 CONT
2 CONT During the later years of the reign of his half-brother, Gruffyd, the English had brought Wales into at least nominal subjection. Gruffyd was killed by the English 5 Aug 1063. Bleddyn and his brother Rhiwallon, having submitted to
2 CONC  King Edward, were made rules of Gwynedd and Powys. The Normans who came with William the Conqueror soon encroached upon the Welsh who resisted them and Rhiwallon was slain in battle in 1070. Bleddyn was then the sole Ruler. [The 
2 CONC Weaver Genealogy]
2 CONT
2 CONT ___________________________
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1075, Bleddyn was killed by Rhys, the brother of Maredudd ab Owain, and Rhys in turn was likeed in 1078 by Caradog ap Gruffudd. Bleddyn's kingdom passed to his cousin, Trahaearn ap Caradog, but Trahaearn was killed, along with 
2 CONC Caradog ap Gruffudd, in the battle of Mynydd Carn in 1081. [A History of Wales; John Davies]
2 CONT
2 CONT    Marriage Information:
2 CONT
2 CONT Bleddyn married Haer FERCH CYNILLIN, daughter of Cynillin AP Y BLAIDD RYDD and Unknown, in 1044. (Haer FERCH CYNILLIN was born about 1025 in Gest near Penmorfa, Caernarvonshire, Wales and died after 1050.)
2 CONT
2 CONT     Marriage Information:
2 CONT
2 CONT Bleddyn also married Miss FERCH BROCHWEL, daughter of Brochwel AP BLEDRUS and Unknown, before 1058 in 2nd wife. (Miss FERCH BROCHWEL was born about 1040 in Anglesey, Wales.)
