2 TITL An Esteemed Lineage
1 NOTE BIOGRAPHY: During the later years of the reign of his half-brother, Gruffyd, the English had brought Wales into at least nominal subjection. Gruffyd was killed by the English August 5, 1063. 
2 CONT
2 CONT BIOGRAPHY: Bleddyn and his brother Rhiwallon, having submitted to King Edward, 
2 CONT were made rulers of Gwynedd and Powys. The Normans who came with 
2 CONT William the Conqueror soon encroached upon the Welsh who resisted them and Rhiwallon was slain in battle in 1070. Bleddyn was then the sole ruler. [Source: The Weaver Genealogy, p 46] 
1 NOTE "AP CYNFYN"; PRINCE OF POWYS; KING OF WALES 1063-1075
1 NOTE [De La Pole.FTW]
2 CONT Sources: Llantarnam Abbey; Young; Kraentzler 1408; Dictionary of National Biography.
2 CONT    Young: Bleddyn ap Cynfyn, prince of Powys, died 1075.   K: Bleddyn ap Cynvyn, Prince of Powis, "A wise and gentle ruler."
2 CONT                            ************ SOURCES:  1.  _Dictionary of National Biography_.  Gives many of his descendants on
2 CONT       page 308.  2.  Bartrum, Peter C.  _Welsh Genealogies, AD 300-1400_.  University of
2 CONT       Wales Press, 1978; "Bleddyn ap Cynfyn 1", page 28.
1 NOTE [De La Pole.FTW]
2 CONT Sources: Llantarnam Abbey; Young; Kraentzler 1408; Dictionary of National Biography.
2 CONT    Young: Bleddyn ap Cynfyn, prince of Powys, died 1075.   K: Bleddyn ap Cynvyn, Prince of Powis, "A wise and gentle ruler."
2 CONT                            ************ SOURCES:  1.  _Dictionary of National Biography_.  Gives many of his descendants on
2 CONT       page 308.  2.  Bartrum, Peter C.  _Welsh Genealogies, AD 300-1400_.  University of
2 CONT       Wales Press, 1978; "Bleddyn ap Cynfyn 1", page 28.
1 NOTE [De La Pole.FTW]
2 CONT Sources: Llantarnam Abbey; Young; Kraentzler 1408; Dictionary of National Biography.
2 CONT    Young: Bleddyn ap Cynfyn, prince of Powys, died 1075.   K: Bleddyn ap Cynvyn, Prince of Powis, "A wise and gentle ruler."
2 CONT                            ************ SOURCES:  1.  _Dictionary of National Biography_.  Gives many of his descendants on
2 CONT       page 308.  2.  Bartrum, Peter C.  _Welsh Genealogies, AD 300-1400_.  University of
2 CONT       Wales Press, 1978; "Bleddyn ap Cynfyn 1", page 28.
1 NOTE
2 CONT
2 CONT REFN: 6785The half-brother of Gruffydd ap Llywelyn of Deheubarth, Bleddynfaced the advance of the Normans after the conquest in 1066. He gavesupport to the Mercians, assisting Edric "the Wild" in 1067 and Edwin andMorcar in 1068. 
2 CONC In 1070, at the battle of mechain, he slew two sons ofGruffydd who challenged his succession, but was subsequently under greatpressure on his north-eastern border from the marcher lords. He waskilled in 1075 by Rhys ap Owain of De
2 CONC heubarth, but his descendantscontinued to rule Powys. The Chronicle of the princes lavished praise onhim as "the most mild and clement of kings".
2 CONT
2 CONT Acceded to the thrown of Powys and Gwynedd in 1063.
2 CONT
2 CONT Source: Oxford Kings & Queens of Britian, John Cannon and Anne Hargreaves.
