1 NOTE 1  NAME Tewdwr Mawr "the Great" Ap /Cadell/ 2  SOUR S033320 3  DATA 4  TEXT Date of Import: Jan 17, 2001
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT [De La Pole.FTW]
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources: Young; Kraentzler 1446; History of Morgan Family.
2 CONT    Also Twdwr, Tewdwr-Mawr, Tudor, Tewdor, Theodore.
2 CONT    Young: Tewdr Mawr, prince of Deheubarth.
2 CONT    History:   "Twdwr-Mawr gave his name to the Twdwr (Tudor) family of Wales from which the name Henry Tudor, who established the Tudor line of English monarchs when he ascended the throne as King Henry VII after the Battle of Bos
2 CONC worth Field. (The dynasty also included King Henry VII and Queen Elizabeth I). One of Twdwr-Mawr's sons was Rhys." Died 994.   K: Tudor ap Cadwell. Slain at Pen Rhys in 1089. Lotsa difference re death.                          ***
2 CONC ***** His name is variously given as Twdwr, Tewdwr-Mawr, Tudor, Tewdor, Theodore.
2 CONT
2 CONT SOURCES:  1.  Bartrum, Peter C.  _Welsh Genealogies, AD 300-1400_.  University of
2 CONT       Wales Press, 1978; "Tewdwr Mawr".
2 CONT   2.  Morgan, Dennis.  _A History of the Morgan Family_.
