1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Please see Darrell Wolcott: The Consorts and Children of Gruffudd ap Llewelyn; http://www.ancientwalesstudies.org/id210.html. (Steven Ferry, July 22, 2020.)
2 CONT
2 CONT -------------------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Bernard de Neufmarché married '''Nesta''' (Agnes), daughter and heir of Osbern fitz Richard, granddaughter of Welsh King Gruffudd ap Llywelyn. Through Nesta, Bernard acquired Bodenham & Berrington, Herefordshire.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Medieval Lands 
2 CONT UNTITLED ENGLISH NOBILITY D - K
2 CONT v5.0 Updated 22 October 2025
2 CONT FITZRICHARD
2 CONT http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/enguntdk.htm#NestAgnesMBernardNeufmarche
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT No trace has been found in sources in Normandy of "Scrob" whose son Richard is shown below.  The name of Richard’s son Osbern suggests that the family was of Viking origin. 
2 CONT
2 CONT a)         OSBERN FitzRichard (-after [1087/88]).  Domesday Book records “Osbern fitzRichard Scrob” holding numerous properties in Worcestershire; several properties in Herefordshire; … m NESTA, daughter of GRUFFYDD ap Llywellyn P
2 CONC rince of Gwynedd and Powys & his second wife Ealdgyth of Mercia.  …
2 CONT
2 CONT Osbern & his wife had three children: 
2 CONT
2 CONT iii)        '''NESTA''' [Agnes] .  A manuscript narrating the history of Brecknock priory records that the founder “Bernard de Nefmarche, Norman” married “Neste qe fut apele Agnes, la file Griffin le fiz Lewelin…cruel tyrant de Ga
2 CONC les”[789], although this skips a generation.  Her parentage and marriage are confirmed by Orderic Vitalis who records that “Osbernus, Ricardi cognomento Scrop filius et Bernardus de Nov Mercato gener eius” committed excesses “in t
2 CONC erritorio Wigornensi”, dated to [1087/88] from the context[790].  The Historia fundationis cum fundatoris genealogia of the priory of Abergavenny names “Sibillam, legitimam hæredem totius terræ Breconiæ…Bernardi et Agnetis de Novo
2 CONC -Mercato” as parents of “Sibillam, legitimam hæredem totius terræ Breconiæ” who married “Milonem”[791].  The Chronicle of Battle Abbey records that "Bernardus cognomento de Novo Mercato…uxor Agnes" donated property in Brecknock to
2 CONC  Battle abbey[792]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT m BERNARD de Neufmarché, son of GEOFFROY de Neufmarché & his wife Ada --- (-1125).  “Bernardus de Novo-mercato” donated property to Breckon priory, for the soul of “Philippi filii mei”, by charter dated to the reign of King Henry 
2 CONC I[793].  Florence of Worcester records that "Beornardus de Novo Mercatu, Rogerius de Laceio…Rawlfus de Mortuo Mari…cum hominibus comitis Rogeri de Scrobbesbyria" threatened Worcester with an army of Normans and Welsh, dated to [10
2 CONC 88][794]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Family
2 CONT
2 CONT http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/WALES.htm#BernardNeufmarchedied1125
2 CONT
2 CONT Bernard & his wife had three children: 
2 CONT * a)         PHILIP .  “Bernardus de Novo-mercato” donated property to Brecknock priory, for the soul of “Philippi filii mei”, by charter dated to the reign of King Henry I[935].  
2 CONT * b)         MAEL .  A manuscript narrating the history of Brecknock priory records that the founder “Bernard de Nefmarche, Norman” married “Neste qe fut apele Agnes, la file Griffin le fiz Lewelin…cruel tyrant de Gales” by whom h
2 CONC e fathered “Mael…noble chevalier” whom it was claimed was not his son and who was deprived of Brecknock in favour of “la file [de] Neste, Sibile” wife of “Miles…fiz Watir le conestable de Gloucestre e de Hereford”[936].  
2 CONT * c)         SIBYLLE de Neufmarché (-bur Lanthony Prior, Gloucester).  A charter dated to [10 Apr/29 May] 1121 records the arrangements for the marriage of "Miloni de Gloec" and "Sibilia filia Beorndi de Novo Mercato", the dowry b
2 CONC eing all the possessions of her father and of her mother[937].  … m ([Apr/May] 1121) MILES of Gloucester, son of WALTER of Gloucester & his wife Berthe --- (-24 Dec 1143, bur Lanthony Priory, Gloucester).  
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Nesta of Hereford married Bernard de Neufmarché , Lord of Brecknock, son of Geoffrey de Neufmarché and Ada of Hugleville, before 1104.
2 CONT
2 CONT =<nowiki>--------------------</nowiki>=
2 CONT Nesta ferch Gruffydd (born c.1062), married Osbern FitzRichard of Richard's Castle, Shropshire, son of Richard Fitz Scrope, by whom she had issue, including a son, Hugh FitzOsbern who married Eustache de Say, and a daughter Nesta 
2 CONC (Agnes) ferch Osbern, who, sometime before 1099, married Bernard de Neufmarche, Lord of Brecon. The Barons de Braose of Abergavenny descend from Sybil of Neufmarche, the daughter of Bernard and Nesta (Agnes), whose own daughter, B
2 CONC ertha of Hereford married William de Braose, Third Lord of Bramber.
2 CONT =<nowiki>--------------------</nowiki>=
2 CONT
2 CONT See "My Lines"
2 CONT ( http://homepages.rootsweb.ancestry.com/~cousin/html/p58.htm#i7141 )
2 CONT from Compiler: R. B. Stewart, Evans, GA ( http://homepages.rootsweb.ancestry.com/~cousin/html/index.htm ) Aka: Nesta fil Trahern, Nest verch Trahearn, Nesta of Hereford, Nesta ap Griffith.
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Nest Verch Osborn was born c. 1079 to Osbern Fitzrichard and Nest Verch Gruffydd.  Nest married Bernard De Neufmarche and had a child:  Sybil (Sybile) De Neufmarche.
2 CONT
2 CONT Nest Verch Osborn De Neufmarche is my 30th great grandmother.
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT according to [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gruffydd_ap_Llywelyn#Marriage_and_issue '''wiki''']: She had 7 children (not named)
2 CONT ----www.findagrave.com
2 CONT
2 CONT Nest verch Osborn VVETERAN
2 CONT BIRTH 1081
2 CONT England
2 CONT DEATH 1163 (aged 81–82)
2 CONT Wales
2 CONT BURIAL
2 CONT Gloucester Cathedral
2 CONT Gloucester, City of Gloucester, Gloucestershire, England 
2 CONT MEMORIAL ID 233453934
2 CONT
2 CONT Possibly known as Agnes. Her dowry included Berrington and Little Hereford.
2 CONT
