2 CONC h and Foreign: With English and French Glossaries, Volume 1 by John Woodward, George Burnett W. & A. K. Johnston, 1892 - Devices (Heraldry). - 858 pages.  Argent, a cross patonce gules, is the coat of Colville, and Carlyle. With t
2 CONC he charge sable it is borne by Baxeshire, or Banester; and azure, by the Barons of Malpas.  
