2 CONT from  [http://www.ancientwalesstudies.org/id152.html THE "MALPAS" FAMILY IN CHESHIRE] By Darrell Wolcott
2 CONT
2 CONT (a) Pedigrees identify him as holding a moiety of Malpas, or one-half.  He would have inheirited 1/3 from his mother, being Ralph's part, and 1/6 from his father, being half of William II's part.  His brother, William III held the
2 CONC  other 1/6, which descended to Dan David.  The final 1/3 of Malpas was held by the line '''descended from David of 1060'''.  The daughter of Ralph shown in our chart, was not an heiress; she had a brother named David who inherited
2 CONC  the final 1/3 
2 CONT
2 CONT (d) A younger brother of William II ap Sir William in CHART 1
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT When we correctly identify the people named in the 3 citations, we would have:
2 CONT
2 CONT *              b.  Ralph ap Einion ap '''Dafydd ap Sir William''', born c. 1125, married Beatrix, born c. 1135, a daughter of Ranulf de Gernon, 4th Earl of Chester, and sister of Hugh Cyfeiliog.
2 CONT
