1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ----
2 CONT ===Biography 
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sibyl_de_Neufmarche (retrieved 20 November 2025)
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Sibyl de Neufmarché''', Countess of Hereford, suo jure Lady of Brecknock (c. 1100 – after 1143), was a Cambro-Norman noblewoman, heiress to one of the most substantial fiefs in the Welsh Marches. The great-granddaughter of [htt
2 CONC ps://www.geni.com/people/Gruffydd-ap-Llewelyn-King-of-Wales/6000000000115658866?through=6000000003649687931 Gruffydd ap Llywelyn], king of Wales, Sibyl was also connected to the nobility of England and Normandy. Sibyl inherited th
2 CONC e titles and lands of her father, Bernard de Neufmarché, Lord of Brecon, after her mother, Nest ferch Osbern, had declared her brother Mahel to have been illegitimate. Most of these estates passed to Sibyl's husband, Miles de Glou
2 CONC cester, 1st Earl of Hereford, as her dowry. Their marriage had been arranged personally by King Henry I of England in the spring of 1121. Sibyl, with her extensive lands, was central to the King's plans of consolidating Anglo-Norm
2 CONC an power in south-east Wales by the merging of her estates with those of Miles, his loyal subject on whom he relied to implement Crown policy.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Sybil de Neufmarché was sole heiress of Bernard de Newmarch.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sybil was our ancestor through three distinct descent lines--through her daughter Bertha, through her daughter Lucia, and through her daughter Margaret, each of whom was independently our ancestor.
2 CONT
2 CONT See "My Lines"
2 CONT
2 CONT ( http://homepages.rootsweb.ancestry.com/~cousin/html/p58.htm#i7135 )
2 CONT
2 CONT from Compiler: R. B. Stewart, Evans, GA
2 CONT
2 CONT ( http://homepages.rootsweb.ancestry.com/~cousin/html/index.htm )
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT 	Neufmarche
2 CONT
2 CONT Geoffrey de Neufmarche b abt 1045. He md Ada de Heugleville abt 1066, daughter of Richard de Heugleville and Ada. She was b abt 1052.
2 CONT
2 CONT Child of Geoffrey de Neufmarche and Ada de Heugleville was:
2 CONT
2 CONT Bernard de Neufmarche, Lord of Brecon, b abt 1074, d 1125. He md Nesta abt 1095, daughter of Osborn Fitz Richard and Nesta verch Gruffydd.
2 CONT
2 CONT Child of Bernard de Neufmarche and Nesta was:
2 CONT
2 CONT Sibyl de Neufmarche b abt 1104, Aberhonwy, Wales, d aft 1143, Gloucestershire, England. She md Sir Miles Fitz Walter, Earl of Hereford, Constable, abt May 1121, son of Walter Fitz Roger of Gloucester, Constable of Gloucester Castl
2 CONC e, and Berthe.
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Sole heiress of her father.
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Sole heiress of her father. First name aka 'Sybyl'.
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Sybile De Neufmarche was born c. 1100 in Brecon Castle, Brecon, Wales to Bernard De Neufmarche, Lord of Brecon and Nest ferch Osbern De Neufmarche.  Sybile married Miles de Gloucester, 1st Earl of Herford in the spring of 1121 and
2 CONC  had 8 children:  Margaret of Hereford; Roger Fitzmiles, 2nd Earl of Hereford; Walter de Hereford; Henry Fitzmiles; Mahel de Hereford; William de Hereford; Bertha of Hereford; and Lucy of Hereford.  She passed away AFTER 1143 in L
2 CONC lanthony Secunda Priory, Glocester, England and is buried in Llanthony Secunda Priory, Glocester, England.
2 CONT
2 CONT NOTE:  See link:
2 CONT
2 CONT [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sibyl_de_Neufmarch%C3%A9]
2 CONT
2 CONT Sybile de Neufmarche de Gloucester is my 29th great grandmother.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Sibyl de Neufmarché, Countess of Hereford, suo jure Lady of Brecknock (c. 1100 – after 1143), was a Cambro-Norman noblewoman, heiress to one of the most substantial fiefs in the Welsh Marches. The great-granddaughter of Gruffydd a
2 CONC p Llywelyn, king of Wales, Sibyl was also connected to the nobility of England and Normandy. Sibyl inherited the titles and lands of her father, Bernard de Neufmarché, Lord of Brecon, after her mother, Nest ferch Osbern, had decla
2 CONC red her brother Mahel to have been illegitimate. Most of these estates passed to Sibyl's husband, Miles de Gloucester, 1st Earl of Hereford, as her dowry. Their marriage had been arranged personally by King Henry I of England in t
2 CONC he spring of 1121
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT By the time of his death around 1125, Bernard (Sibyl's father) had established a flourishing borough around his castle of Brecon. Henry I had married Bernard's daughter '''Sibyl''' to Miles Fitz Walter, the High Sheriff of Glouces
2 CONC tershire, in 1121 and passed a significant portion of Bernard's honour to him as a dowry, including Hay-on-Wye Castle.
2 CONT
2 CONT According to Giraldus Cambrensis this was because Mahel de Neufmarché the son and heir of Bernard had mutilated the paramour of his mother. In vengeance his mother, Nesta, swore to King Henry I that her son was illegitimate. Henry
2 CONC  was therefore able by law and custom to pass over Mahel and give the land to his friend and confident Miles Fitz Walter with Bernard's legal heiress in marriage.
2 CONT www.findagrave.com
2 CONT
