1 NOTE "AP CYNAN"; PRINCE OF NORTH WALES; RULER OF GWYNEDD (NORTH WALES); KING
2 CONT 1081-1137; HAD ADDITIONAL 2 SONS & 4 DAUGHTERS BESIDES THOSE SHOWN
1 NOTE He ruled from 1055 to 1137. He was the ruler of North Wales and spent much of the first twelve years of his reign imprisoned in England by order of King William, the Conqueror. His imprisonment continued during the first six years
2 CONC  of William Rufus. His sons succeeded him, but they were styled Princes, not Kings.
1 NOTE Source "The Rufus Parks Pedigree" by Brian J.L. Berry.
2 CONT
2 CONT Page 79 Chart:   Gruffyd 1081-1137
2 CONT
2 CONT !Availability: The libraries of Ken, Kevin, Karen, Kristen, Brian, Adam, Amy, and FAL.
2 CONT
2 CONT Source: "Ancestral Roots of Sixty Colonists" by Frederick Lewis Weis
2 CONT
2 CONT Page 197, Line: (239-5):
2 CONT
2 CONT 5.    GRIFFITH, b. Dublin 1055, d. 1137, Prince of North Wales; m. ca. 1095, ANGHARAT  of Regaingl, dau. OWAIN ap EDWIN.
2 CONT
