1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ====Medilands (''16 Nov 2021'') Brittany Nobility: Cournouaille, Panthièvre [http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/brittcope.htm#EudesIdied1062B Comtes de Panthièvre]====
2 CONT
2 CONT '''EUDES de Bretagne''', son of GEOFFROY I Duke of Brittany & his wife Havise de Normandie (-Cesson 1079, bur Saint-Brieuc).  
2 CONT >Guillaume of Jumièges names ''“Emma...secunda Hadvis...tertia Mathildis''” as the three daughters of Richard and his wife “''Gunnor ex nobilissima Danorum prosapia ortam''”, adding that Havise married “''Goiffredo Britannorum com
2 CONC iti''” by whom she had “''Alanum et Eudonem duces''”[322].  
2 CONT >A charter dated 1008 records that, after the death of "''Gaufrido comite Britanniæ", "filii eius Alanus et Eudo cum matre eorum Hadeguisia''" restored the abbey of Saint-Méen[323].  "''Alanus et Egio Britannorum monarchi''" found
2 CONC ed the priory of Livré "''in pago Redonensi''" by charter dated to [1013/22], signed by "…''Aduise matre eorum comitum, Rivalloni vicarii, Triscanni''…"[324].  
2 CONT >A charter dated 1026 recalls that "''Gaufridus, Conani Curvi filius''" was killed "''apud Concuruz prelium''", recalling that "''quo defuncto, Alanus filius eius…renum patris suscipiens''", witnessed by "''Alanus comes…Heudo frat
2 CONC er eius''"[325].  
2 CONT >He appears to have ruled Brittany jointly with his brother until the death of their mother in 1034.  Following disputes with his brother, a division of territories was agreed, Eudes taking the dioceses of Dol, Saint Malo, Saint B
2 CONC rieuc and Tréguier, at which time he can be said to have become Comte de Penthièvre.  
2 CONT >"''Manigenius…miles''" founded the priory of Saint-Cyr-lès-Rennes and donated it to Tours Saint-Julien by charter dated 23 May 1037, subscribed by "''Alanus dux…Eudonis fratris Alani ducis Britannorum, Gotzelini vicecomitis, Rual
2 CONC entis domini Doli''…"[326].  
2 CONT >After the death of his brother in 1040, Eudes seized Brittany and excluded his nephew, succeeding as EUDES I Duke of Brittany.  According to Orderic Vitalis, Eudes ruled the country "freely without acknowledging any lord for 15 y
2 CONC ears"[327].  However, his nephew retaliated, captured Eudes and imprisoned him in chains[328].  
2 CONT >"''Comes Eudo et nepos eius Gaufridus, Robertus vicecomes et frater eius Eudo…Guichomarus filius Alani vicecomitis''…" witnessed a charter dated to 1050 relating to the abbey of Saint-Georges de Rennes[329].  
2 CONT >"''Comes Eudo, uxor eius Orguen et filii eorum Gausfridus, Alanus, Willelmus, Rotbertus, Ricardus''…" witnessed the charter dated to [1056/60] records the history of the acquisition by Angers Saint-Aubin of property "''in pago Be
2 CONC lvacensi''", finally donated by "''comiti Britannie Eudoni''"[330].  
2 CONT >The ''Chronicon Britannico'' records the death in 1079 of "''Eudo Dux Britanniæ''"[331].  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m ORGUEN [Agnes] de Cornouaïlle''', daughter of ALAIN "''Caignard''" Comte de Cornouaïlle & his wife Judith de Nantes .  "''Comes Eudo, uxor eius Orguen et filii eorum Gausfridus, Alanus, Willelmus, Rotbertus, Ricardus''…" witn
2 CONC essed the charter dated to [1056/60] records the history of the acquisition by Angers Saint-Aubin of property "in pago Belvacensi", finally donated by "''comiti Britannie Eudoni''"[332]. The primary source which confirms her paren
2 CONC tage has not yet been identified.  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Mistresses (1) - (x): ---'''.  The names of Eudes's mistresses are not known.  
2 CONT
2 CONT >'''Comte Eudes & his wife had six children:'''
2 CONT >>1. GEOFFROY "Boterel" de Bretagne (-killed in battle Dol 24 Aug [1091/93], bur Saint-Brieuc)....
2 CONT >>2. ALAIN "Rufus/the Red" de Bretagne (-4 Aug 1093, bur Bury St Edmunds)....
2 CONT >>3. GUILLAUME de Bretagne....
2 CONT >>4. ROBERT de Bretagne (-after 1083)....
2 CONT >>5. RICHARD de Bretagne....
2 CONT >>6. ÉTIENNE de Bretagne....
