1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 
2 CONT Ednyfed Fychan (c. 1170 – 1246), full name Ednyfed Fychan ap Cynwrig,
2 CONT
2 CONT  was a Welsh warrior who became Seneschal to the Kingdom of Gwynedd in Northern Wales, serving Llywelyn the Great and his son Dafydd ap Llywelyn. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Ednyfed claimed descent from Marchudd ap Cynan, Lord of Rhos, 'protector' of Rhodri Mawr, King of Gwynedd.  
2 CONT
2 CONT He was the patrilineal 
2 CONT
2 CONT Ancestor of Owen Tudor and thereby of the Tudor dynasty
2 CONT
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ednyfed_Fychan
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Please see Darrell Wolcott: "Bartrum's Pedigrees of the Welsh Tribal Patriarchs" - #23 - Marchweithian, http://www.ancientwalesstudies.org/id193.html. (Steven Ferry, March 19, 2017.)
2 CONT
2 CONT Please see Darrell Wolcott: Llowarch ap Bran - A Pedigree with Problems; http://www.ancientwalesstudies.org/id32.html. (Steven Ferry, April 14, 2017.)
2 CONT
2 CONT Please see Darrell Wolcott: Edwin of Tegeingl and His Family - Aldud ap Owain of Tegeingl; http://www.ancientwalesstudies.org/id83.html. (Steven Ferry, April 19, 2017.)
2 CONT
2 CONT Please see Darrell Wolcott: Angharad, Heiress of Mostyn; http://www.ancientwalesstudies.org/id84.html. (Steven Ferry, April 21, 2107.)
2 CONT
2 CONT Please see Darrell Wolcott: Hwfa ap Cynddelw, Lord of Llifon: http://www.ancientwalesstudies.org/id322.html (Steven Ferry, January 23, 2024.)
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
