2 CONC 355. Jump up ^ Bezzant Lowe, Walter (1912), p358. Jump up ^ Bezzant Lowe, Walter (1912), Chapter V11 pp.354ff. Jump up ^ Bezzant Lowe, Walter (1912), p357. The translation from the Welsh is credited to Mrs Watts-Jones of Glyn, Dyg
2 CONC wyfylchi. Presumably this folk tale was handed down through the ages; a similar tale exists for the medieval poet Einion ap Gwalchmai. Although it is possible that Ednyfed went on a crusade, the tale itself belongs to the realm of
