2 CONT Sources: History of Morgan Family and Dictionary of National Biography.
2 CONT    Married (1) Cadwgan ap Bleddyn and (2) Gruffydd ap Rhys.   In 1136, Gruffydd ap Rhys, under attack in Gower, hurried into North Wales to obtain assistance from his brothers-in-law. His wife, meanwhile, "like an Amazon and a sec
2 CONC ond Penthesilea," commanded his followers in the south. She was slain in battle by Maurice of London, Lord of Kidwelly. Morgan, one of her youthful sons by Gruffydd, perished with her, and a second, Maelgwn, was taken prisoner. Bu
2 CONC t Owain and Cadwaladr, sons of Gruffydd ap Cynan, now came down from the north, destroyed Aberstwith Castle, and in the second week of October they fought along with Gruffydd ap Rhys a great battle near Aberteivi (Cardigan), in wh
2 CONC ich they won a decided victory over Stephen, constable of Aberteivi and "all the Flemings, all the marchers, and all the French from Abernedd to Aberteivi." Quoted material from Dictionary.                         ***** Gruffydd a
2 CONC p Rhys, Prince of Deheubarth...m. shortly after 1116, Gwenllian (killed 1136 while leading an attack on the troops of Maurice de Londres, lord of Kidwelly, where the field of battle is called Maes Gwenllian), daughter of the royal
2 CONC  house of Gwynedd (whose mother was Ragnhildr, dau of the royal house of the Scandinavians of Dublin)...  [Source 1]
2 CONT Married (1) Cadwgan ap Bleddyn and (2) Gruffydd ap Rhys.  In 1136, Gruffydd ap Rhys, under attack in Gower, hurried into North Wales to obtain assistance fromhis brothers-in-law.  His wife, meanwhile, "like an Amazon and a second 
2 CONC Penthesilea," commanded his followers in the south.  She was slain in battle by Maurice of London, Lord of Kidwelly.  Morgan, one of her youthful sons by Gruffydd, perished with her, and a second, Maelgwn, was taken prisoner. But 
2 CONC Owain and Cadwaladr, sons of Gruffydd ap Cynan, now came down from the north, destroyed Aberystwyth Castle, and in the second week of October, they fought along with Gruffydd ap Rhys a great battle near Aberteivi (Cardigan), in wh
2 CONC ich they won a decided victory over Stephen, constable of Aberteivi, and "all the Flemings, all the marchers, and all the French from Abernedd to Aberteivi." [Sources 2 and 3; quotes from Source 3]
2 CONT
2 CONT SOURCES:  1.  Burke, Sir Bernard, C.B., LL.D., Ulster King of Arms.  _Landed Gentry_
2 CONT       (entry under Powell), page 577.
2 CONT   2.  Morgan, Dennis.  _A History of the Morgan Family_.
