4 CONT 1 The book of the generation of Jesus Christ, the son of David, the son of Abraham.
4 CONT
4 CONT 2 Abraham begat Isaac; and Isaac begat Jacob; and Jacob begat Judas and his brethren;
4 CONT
4 CONT 3 And Judas begat Phares and Zara of Thamar; and Phares begat Esrom; and Esrom begat Aram;
4 CONT
4 CONT 4 And Aram begat Aminadab; and Aminadab begat Naasson; and Naasson begat Salmon;
4 CONT
4 CONT 5 And Salmon begat Booz of Rachab; and Booz begat Obed of Ruth; and Obed begat Jesse;
4 CONT
4 CONT 6 And Jesse begat David the king; and David the king begat Solomon of her that had been the wife of Urias;
4 CONT
4 CONT 7 And Solomon begat Roboam; and Roboam begat Abia; and Abia begat Asa;
4 CONT
4 CONT 8 And Asa begat Josaphat; and Josaphat begat Joram; and Joram begat Ozias;
4 CONT
4 CONT 9 And Ozias begat Joatham; and Joatham begat Achaz; and Achaz begat Ezekias;
4 CONT
4 CONT 10 And Ezekias begat Manasses; and Manasses begat Amon; and Amon begat Josias;
4 CONT
4 CONT 11 And Josias begat Jechonias and his brethren, about the time they were carried away to Babylon:
4 CONT
4 CONT 12 And after they were brought to Babylon, Jechonias begat Salathiel; and Salathiel begat Zorobabel;
4 CONT
4 CONT 13 And Zorobabel begat Abiud; and Abiud begat Eliakim; and Eliakim begat Azor;
4 CONT
4 CONT 14 And Azor begat Sadoc; and Sadoc begat Achim; and Achim begat Eliud;
4 CONT
4 CONT 15 And Eliud begat Eleazar; and Eleazar begat Matthan; and Matthan begat Jacob;
4 CONT
4 CONT 16 And Jacob begat Joseph the husband of Mary, of whom was born Jesus, who is called Christ.
4 CONT
4 CONT 17 So all the generations from Abraham to David are fourteen generations; and from David until the carrying away into Babylon are fourteen generations; and from the carrying away into Babylon unto Christ are fourteen generations.
4 CONT
4 CONT 18 Now the birth of Jesus Christ was on this wise: When as his mother Mary was espoused to Joseph, before they came together, she was found with child of the Holy Ghost.
4 CONT
4 CONT 19 Then Joseph her husband, being a just man, and not willing to make her a public example, was minded to put her away privily.
4 CONT
4 CONT 20 But while he thought on these things, behold, the angel of the Lord appeared unto him in a dream, saying, Joseph, thou son of David, fear not to take unto thee Mary thy wife: for that which is conceived in her is of the Holy Gh
4 CONC ost.
4 CONT
4 CONT 21 And she shall bring forth a son, and thou shalt call his name Jesus: for he shall save his people from their sins.
4 CONT
4 CONT 22 Now all this was done, that it might be fulfilled which was spoken of the Lord by the prophet, saying,
4 CONT
4 CONT 23 Behold, a virgin shall be with child, and shall bring forth a son, and they shall call his name Emmanuel, which being interpreted is, God with us.
4 CONT
4 CONT 24 Then Joseph being raised from sleep did as the angel of the Lord had bidden him, and took unto him his wife:
4 CONT
4 CONT 25 And knew her not till she had brought forth her firstborn son: and he called his name Jesus.
