2 CONT [De La Pole.FTW]
2 CONT Sources: History of the Morgan Family; Dictionary of National Biography.
2 CONT    King of South Wales, 1158.   "Born in Ireland and known in Welsh history as Yr Arglwydd Rhys,' The Lord Rhys. Married Gwenillian, daughter of Meda ap Meredith, Prince of Powys. Rhys won recognition of his crown from King Henry 
2 CONC II in 1158 and built Dynevor Castle. He had a daughter Gwenillian and sons Hywel, Griffith, Rhys, Cynwrig and Meredith. Rhys is buried at St. David's Cathedral. The Morgan family connection with the Royal Family of Britain derives
2 CONC  from Lord Rhys."                              ****** King of South Wales, 1158.
2 CONT
2 CONT SOURCES:  1.  Bartrum, Peter C.  _Welsh Genealogies, AD 300-1400_.  University of
2 CONT       Wales Press, 1978; "Rhys ap Tewdwr 4", page 779.
2 CONT   2.  Morgan, Dennis.  _A History of the Morgan Family_.
2 CONT   3.  _Dictionary of National Biography_.
2 CONT Reigned BET. 1155 - 1197 In 1158 Submitted to Henry II and dropped title of King, being Known as the Lord Rhys
