2 CONT From correspondence with Darrell Wolcott re: this man's, and his father's, name : "There are 6 early citations which mention this family.  5 of those cite "Kuan" and the other spells it "Kian".  Likewise, 5 citations cite "Kadian"
2 CONC  and one says "Kadien".  The Welsh alphabet has no letter "K", its sound is represented by the letter "C".  Neither of those names occur in any other known Welsh family. It is possible that all 6 sources drew from a single now-los
2 CONC t source where the handwriting was poor and the intended names were the common names you suggest.  I prefer to not be the first to "correct" the spelling."  (Steven Ferry, September 24, 2019.)
2 CONT
