1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Bertha of Hereford
2 CONT
2 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
2 CONT
2 CONT Bertha of Hereford, also known as Bertha de Pitres (born c.1130), was the daughter of Miles de Gloucester, 1st Earl of Hereford, and a wealthy heiress. She was the wife of William de Braose, Third Lord of Bramber to whom she broug
2 CONC ht many castles and Lordships, including Brecknock, Abergavenny, and Hay.
2 CONT
2 CONT Abergavenny Castle in Monmouthshire, Wales, was one of the castles Bertha of Hereford brought to her husband William de Braose, Third Lord of Bramber
2 CONT
2 CONT Family
2 CONT
2 CONT Bertha was born in England in about 1130. She was the second daughter[1] of Miles of Gloucester, 1st Earl of Hereford (1097- 24 December 1143) and Sibyl of Neufmarche. She had two sisters, Margaret of Gloucester, who married Humph
2 CONC rey de Bohun, by whom she had issue, and Lucy of Gloucester, who married Herbert FitzHerbert of Winchester, by whom she had issue. Her five brothers, included Roger Fitzmiles, 2nd Earl of Hereford, Walter de Hereford, Henry Fitzmi
2 CONC les, William de Hereford, and Mahel de Hereford.[2]
2 CONT
2 CONT Her paternal grandparents were Walter FitzRoger de Pitres, Sheriff of Gloucester and Bertha de Bateden. Her maternal grandparents were Bernard de Neufmarche, Lord of Brecon, and Nesta ferch Osbern. The latter was a daughter of Osb
2 CONC ern FitzRichard of Richard's Castle, and Nesta ferch Gruffydd.[3]Bertha was a direct descendant, in the maternal line, of Gruffydd ap Llywelyn (1007- 5 August 1063) and Edith (Aldgyth), daughter of Elfgar, Earl of Mercia.
2 CONT
2 CONT Her father Miles served as Constable to King Stephen of England. He later served in the same capacity to Empress Matilda after he'd transferred his allegiance. In 1141, she made him Earl of Hereford in gratitude for his loyalty. O
2 CONC n 24 December 1143, he was killed whilst on a hunting expedition.
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage and children
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1150 [MedLands says before 1140 - possibly a contingent betrothal], she married William de Braose, 3rd Lord of Bramber (1112- 1192), son of Philip de Braose, 2nd Lord of Bramber and Aenor, daughter of Judael of Totnes. William 
2 CONC and Bertha had three daughters and two sons, including William de Braose, 4th Lord of Bramber.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1173[4], her brothers all having died without issue, she brought the Lordships and castles of Brecknock and Abergavenny, to her husband. Hay Castle had already passed to her from her mother, Sibyl of Neufmarche in 1165, whence 
2 CONC it became part of the de Braose holdings.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1174, her husband became Sheriff of Hereford.
2 CONT
2 CONT Her children include:
2 CONT
2 CONT    1. William de Braose, 7th Baron Abergavenny, 4th Lord of Bramber (1144/1153- 11 August 1211, Corbeil), married Maud de St. Valery, daughter of Bernard de St. Valery, by whom he had 16 children.
2 CONT
2 CONT    2. Roger de Braose
2 CONT
2 CONT    3. Bertha de Braose (born 1151), married c.1175, Walter de Beauchamp (died 1235), son of William de Beauchamp and Joan de Walerie, by whom she had issue, including Walcherine de Beauchamp who married Joane de Mortimer.
2 CONT
2 CONT    4. Sibylla de Braose (died after 5 February 1227), married William de Ferrers, 3rd Earl of Derby (1136- 21 October 1190 at Acre on crusade), son of Robert de Ferrers, 2nd Earl of Derby and Margaret Peverel, by whom she had issu
2 CONC e.
2 CONT
2 CONT    5. Maud de Braose, married John de Brompton, by whom she had issue.
2 CONT
2 CONT Legacy
2 CONT
2 CONT Bertha died on an unknown date. She is the ancestress of the families de Braose, de Beauchamp, and de Ferrers.
2 CONT
2 CONT References
2 CONT
2 CONT    1. ^ The Complete Peerage, Vol.1, "Abergavenny"
2 CONT
2 CONT    2. ^ The Complete Peerage, Vol.1 "Abergavenny"
2 CONT
2 CONT    3. ^ ThePeerage.com
2 CONT
2 CONT    4. ^ The Complete Peerage, Vol.1 "Abergavenny"
2 CONT
2 CONT [Repetitive Wikipedia texts stripped out]
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Sir Miles Fitz Walter [b], Constable, Earl of Hereford, b abt 1095, of Gloucestershire, England, d 24 Dec 1143. He md Sibyl de Neufmarche abt May 1121, daughter of Sir Bernard de Neufmarche, Lord of Brecon, and Nesta.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Miles Fitz Walter and Sibyl de Neufmarche were:
2 CONT
2 CONT Margaret of Hereford abt 1124, of Gloucester, Gloucestershire, England, d 1146. She md Humphrey III de Bohun abt 1137, son of Sir Humphrey II de Bohun, Constable of England, and Maud of Salisbury.
2 CONT
2 CONT Bertha of Hereford b abt 1128, Gloucestershire, England. She md William de Braose, Lord of Abergavenny, abt Aug 1148, son of Philip de Braose, Lord of Briouze and Bramber, and Aenor de Totnes.
2 CONT
2 CONT Lucy of Hereford b abt 1132, Gloucester, Gloucestershire, England. She md Herbert Fitz Herbert abt 1160, prob Gloucestershire, England, son of Herbert Fitz Herbert and Sibyl Corbet.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
