1 NAME Richard /ap William ap William/
2 GIVN Richard
2 SURN ap William ap William
2 _MARNM ap William ap William
2 NICK Richard de Duckenton
1 NAME Richard "le Belward" de Malpas, of Duckington
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE ABT 1120
2 ADDR
3 CITY Malpas
3 STAE England
1 OCCU
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Please see Darrell Wolcott: The "Malpas" Family in Cheshire; http://www.ancientwalesstudies.org/id152.html. (Steven Ferry, April 19, 2020.)
2 CONT
2 CONT Richard ap William III ap William II ap Sir William was born around 1120.  His mother was Mabel, daughter of Robert-fitz-Hugh, the base son of http://www.geni.com/people/Hugh-Lupus-d-Avranches-1st-Earl-of-Chester/60000000061460161
2 CONC 86?through=6000000000538172995.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was the 3rd son of William "le Belward," and was seated at Duckington.  His older brothers were David & Robert.
2 CONT
2 CONT The name of Richard's wife is not known.
2 CONT
2 CONT Their son William married Beannan, daughter of Ralph ap Einion ap David ap Sir William by Beatrix daughter of Earl Ranulf II of Chester, sister of Hugh Cyfeiliog
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ===notes===
2 CONT From [http://www.thornber.net/cheshire/htmlfiles/littlebud.html Egerton Families of Cheshire]
2 CONT
2 CONT The Egerton family is very widespread across Cheshire and Lancashire with many branches. The following brief account of the eary history attempts to show how some of these groups are related. The Egertons trace their ancestry to J
2 CONC ohn Le Belward of Depenbeche, alias Malpas, in the reign of William Rufus. The surname of Egerton was not assumed until the fifth generation, when Philip purchased Egerton in Cheshire.
2 CONT
2 CONT * 4. Richard, 3rd son of William Le Belward, seated at Duckington.
2 CONT **3. William Le Belward of Malpas, married Beatrix, dau of Hugh Kiveliock Earl of Chester and coheiress of her brother Ranulph.
2 CONT ***2. William Le Belward, married Letitia, [SIC: Mabella] dau. and coheiress of Robert Fitz Hugh first Baron of Malpas.
2 CONT ****1. John Le Belward
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT * [http://www.ancientwalesstudies.org/id152.html THE "MALPAS" FAMILY IN CHESHIRE] By Darrell Wolcott     
2 CONT * [https://books.google.com/books?id=2Gc5AAAAMAAJ&pg=PA17&lpg=PA17&dq=David+Golbourne+de+Malpas&source=bl&ots=M2jG3ixaFP&sig=oxtopzCk1cTtECBlrOUspZNJsrE&hl=en&sa=X&ei=9oMkVbLEHMzzsAXF1oOQBQ&ved=0CCkQ6AEwBA#v=onepage&q=David%20Golb
2 CONC ourne%20de%20Malpas&f=false page 17] of Peerage of England. ... by Arthur Collins Printed for F. C. and J. Rivington, 1812 - England
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
