2 CONT
2 CONT ------------------------------------------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Ifor married Nest, sister of Rhys ap Gruffudd (also known as The Lord Rhys) and was succeeded by his son Gruffudd before 1170. Gruffudd ap Ifor married Mabel FitzRobert, a natural daughter of Robert, Earl of Gloucester, and half s
2 CONC ister of the kidnapped earl. Ifor's descendants included his grandson Morgan Gam and his great-grandson Llywelyn Bren and, through Gruffudd and Mabel.[1] 
2 CONT
2 CONT The Manor of Radyr The mill was originally leased to Griffith, son of Ifor Bach - famed for his raid on Cardiff Castle - from whom the mill took its name.[2] 
2 CONT
2 CONT List of Lords of Senghenydd (Dates of Reign) 
2 CONT
2 CONT Meurig of Senghenydd Ifor Bach (-1170) Gruffudd ap Ifor Bach (1170 - 1211) Rhys ap Gruffudd ap Ifor Bach
2 CONT  Gruffudd ap Rhys Bach (-1268)
2 CONT  Llywelyn Bren (-1318)
2 CONT  Gruffudd ap Llywelyn Bren (1318-1350)
2 CONT  Meurig Bren (1350-1386)
2 CONT  Rhys Bren (1386-1404)
2 CONT  Iolo Bren (1404-1443)
2 CONT  Gwillym Bren (1443-1484)
2 CONT  Gwillym Bren (1484-1502)[3] 
2 CONT
