1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''For the best current source of information on Madoc:''' https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Madoc
2 CONT
2 CONT ''(Excerpt from Wiki):''
2 CONT
2 CONT "Madoc or Madog ab Owain Gwynedd was, according to folklore, a Welsh prince who sailed to America in 1170, over three hundred years before Christopher Columbus's voyage in 1492. According to the story, he was a son of Owain Gwyned
2 CONC d, and took to the sea to flee internecine violence at home. The "Madoc story" legend evidently evolved out of a medieval tradition about a Welsh hero's sea voyage, to which only allusions survive. However, it attained its greates
2 CONC t prominence during the Elizabethan era, when English and Welsh writers wrote of the claim that Madoc had come to the Americas as an assertion of prior discovery, and hence legal possession, of North America by the Kingdom of Engl
2 CONC and."  - WIKI
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Other sources - videos:'''
2 CONT
2 CONT * [https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=kVyr-C_Qaq8 Prince Madog] ''An excellent informative documentary:'' 
2 CONT
2 CONT * [http://www.history.com/topics/exploration/exploration-of-north-america/videos/did-the-welsh-discover-america Did the Welsh Discover America?]
2 CONT
2 CONT * [https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=X1YKuiGqhK4 The Beginning Of America: Who Got To The Shores First?]
2 CONT
2 CONT '''10 Part discussion of Madoc as one of the early explorers and colonizers of the North Americas:'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Part 1: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Aa6c6pqgTK8
2 CONT
2 CONT Part 2: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=IBrbffQ-wqA
