1 NAME Seisyll /ap Dyfnwal/
2 GIVN Seisyll
2 SURN ap Dyfnwal
2 _MARNM ap Dyfnwal
2 NICK Systyl ap Cyfnwall
2 NICK Lord of Upper Gwent
2 NICK Seisyllt
1 NAME Seisyll ap Dyfnwal, Lord of Upper Gwent
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE ABT 1120
2 PLAC Castell Arnallt, Llanofer, Monmouthshire, England
2 ADDR
1 DEAT
2 DATE 25 DEC 1175
2 PLAC Abergavenny, Monmouthshire, Wales
2 ADDR
1 OCCU
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} See Peter Bartrum, https://www.geni.com/documents/view?doc_id=6000000173395392898 (June 21, 2022; Anne Brannen, curator)
2 CONT
2 CONT See Peter Bartrum, https://cadair.aber.ac.uk/dspace/bitstream/handle/2160/5435/Ynyr%20Gwent%203.png?sequence=1&isAllowed=y (January 22, 2020; Anne Brannen, curator)
2 CONT
2 CONT On or about Christmas Day of 1175, William de Braose invited Seisyllt ap Dyfnwal and his followers to a banquet, and had them all murdered; Seisyllt's wife and younger son Cadwaladr, who were at home, were also murdered.  De Braos
2 CONC e's actions were in retaliation, presumably, for Seisyllt's murder of his uncle.  In retaliation for de Braose's actions, King John seized de Braose's lands and imprisoned his wife and son at Windsor, where he starved them to deat
2 CONC h.  See http://welshjournals.llgc.org.uk/browse/viewpage/llgc-id:1337678/llgc-id:1340124/llgc-id:1340148/getText (Feb 25, 2016; Anne Brannen, curator).
2 CONT
2 CONT As reported by the Welsh chroniclers, "from that time forth, after that treachery, none of the Welsh dared place trust in the French." (See Thomas Jones's translation of Peniarth MS 70 (71)).
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Please see Darrell Wolcott; The Welsh Ancestry of the Tudor Dynasty; http://www.ancientwalesstudies.org/id217.html. (Steven Ferry, June 5, 2018.)
2 CONT
2 CONT Please see Darrell Wolcott: Family of Drymbenog ap Maenyrch of Brycheiniog; http://www.ancientwalesstudies.org/id312.html (Steven Ferry, May 21, 2023.)
2 CONT
2 CONT ********************************
2 CONT
2 CONT notes removed that connected Systyl ap Dyfnwall to Dante. profile locked to prevent further merging.
2 CONT --------------------
