1 OCCU 1st Baron of Offaly, (Ancestor of Kildare Branch of FitzGerald Dynasty), Took part in the conquest of the Limerick
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Please see Darrell Wolcott: Osbwrn Wyddel of Cors Gedol; http://www.ancientwalesstudies.org/id203.html. (Steven Ferry, August 30, 2020.)
2 CONT
2 CONT Name: '''Gerald FitzMaurice Fitzgerald'''  
2 CONT
2 CONT Birth: ABT 1150 in Windsor, Berkshire, England 
2 CONT
2 CONT Death: 15 JAN 1202/03 in Offaly, Kildare, Ireland 
2 CONT
2 CONT Note:  Gerald FitzMaurice FitzGerald, 1st Baron of Offaly (not a peerage of Parliament but a designation of the ancestors of the Earls of Kildare); c1150; took part in the conquest of Limerick c1197 and acquired Croom in that Co (
2 CONC hence the wording of the family motto); 
2 CONT
2 CONT married c1193 Eve (married 2nd Geoffrey FitzRobert (d 1211) and 3rd by Feb 1217/8 Geoffrey de Marisco/Mareis, Justiciar of Ireland, and died by Dec 1226), thought to have been daughter of Robert de Bermingham, by which marriage he
2 CONC  acquired the territorial Barony of Offaly (an entity wholly distinct from Ophelan aforementioned), though Offaly was in his wife's 3rd husband Geoffrey de Marisco's hands following her death (it was forfeited by Geoffrey in 1234,
2 CONC  however, and passed to Gerald's heir); Gerald died 1245. [Burke's Peerage]
2 CONT
2 CONT Father: '''Maurice "The Invader" Fitzgerald Of Windsor''' b: ABT 1100 in Castle Carew, Pembrokeshire, Wales  Mother: '''Alice de Montgomery''' b: ABT 1115 in Munster, Ireland
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage 1''' Eve de Bermingham''' b: ABT 1172 in Offaly, Kildare, Ireland
2 CONT
2 CONT Children
2 CONT
2 CONT Maurice Fitzgerald b: ABT 1190 in Offaly, Kildare, Ireland
2 CONT
2 CONT http://wc.rootsweb.ancestry.com/cgi-bin/igm.cgi?op=GET&db=jcrow&id=I18409
2 CONT =<nowiki>--------------------</nowiki>=
2 CONT Gerald FitzMaurice, 1st Lord of Offaly
2 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia Gerald FitzMaurice
2 CONT * Born	c. 1150
2 CONT * Title	1st Lord of Offaly
2 CONT * Tenure	c. 1193 – 1204
2 CONT * Nationality	Cambro-Norman
2 CONT * Locality	Ireland
2 CONT * Successor	Maurice FitzGerald, 2nd Lord of Offaly
2 CONT * Spouse(s)	Eve de Bermingham
2 CONT * Parents	Maurice FitzGerald, Lord of Lanstephan
2 CONT
2 CONT Gerald FitzMaurice, jure uxoris 1st Lord of Offaly (c. 1150 – 15 January 1204) was a Cambro-Norman nobleman who settled in Ireland, with his father, Maurice FitzGerald, Lord of Lanstephan, founding the notable FitzGerald dynasty w
2 CONC ho were to play important roles in Irish history. By right of his wife, the heiress Eve de Bermingham, Gerald was granted the barony of Offaly, thus becoming the first Lord. He is the ancestor of the Kildare branch of the dynasty.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Family===
2 CONT
2 CONT Gerald was born in Wales in about 1150, the second eldest son of Maurice FitzGerald, Lord of Lanstephan and an unknown second wife. Gerald had one sister, Nesta, who was named after their celebrated grandmother, Princess Nest ferc
2 CONC h Rhys, and five brothers, including his eldest, William FitzMaurice, 1st Baron of Naas.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Career===
2 CONT
2 CONT Gerald's father was the leader of the first landing of Normans who arrived in Ireland in 1169 to assist the exiled Irish King of Leinster Dermot MacMurrough regain his kingdom. Both Gerald and his father were at the Siege of Dubli
2 CONC n in 1171.[1] Upon the death of their father, on 1 September 1176, Gerald's elder brother William granted him half the cantred of Ophelan with centres at Maynooth and Rathmore. He was confirmed in them by Prince John in 1185. In 1
2 CONC 197, he took part in the conquest of Limerick acquiring Croom, County Limerick.[2]
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Marriage and issue===
2 CONT
2 CONT Sometime around 1193, he married as her first husband, Eve de Bermingham (died between June 1223 and December 1226), daughter of Sir Robert de Bermingham. In marriage, he received the barony of Offaly, becoming the first FitzGeral
2 CONC d Lord of Offaly. Together Gerald and Eve had one son:
2 CONT * Maurice FitzGerald, 2nd Lord of Offaly, Justiciar of Ireland (1194- 20 May 1257), married Juliana N.N., by whom he had four sons.
2 CONT
2 CONT Following Gerald's death on 15 January 1204, Eve would go on to marry two more times. Her second husband was Geoffrey FitzRobert, and her third, whom she married sometime after 1211, was Geoffrey de Marisco, Justiciar of Ireland.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===References===
2 CONT
