2 CONT Maurice FitzGerald, Lord of Lanstephan
2 CONT
2 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
2 CONT
2 CONT His son Sir Gerald FitzMaurice (c1152 -c1203) married the daughter of Robert de Birmingham. Their son was Sir Maurice FitzGerald, Justiciar of Ireland, Lord of Offaly, (1190 - 1257, died at Youghal. His son was Sir Maurice FitzMau
2 CONC rice Fitz Gerald, Justiciar of Ireland, Lord of Offaly, (c1239, Wexford - 1286, Ross,Ireland)
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT He gained the title of 1st Baron of Offaly [feudal barony]. Circa 1197 he took part in the conquest of Limerick, acquiring Croom, County Limerick.
2 CONT --------------------
