2 CONT 16. Cynan ab Iago [JC.25; GaC]
2 CONT
2 CONT 17. Radnaillt of Dublin [GaC] [Note: The name of the wife of Cynan apIago, her parentage, and her mother's parentage are known only from GaC(and sources dependant on GaC). Although reservations have sometimes beenexpressed regardi
2 CONC ng this information, enough of the data from thepedigrees of Radnaillt are verified in Irish sources that I am inclinedto regard the information as genuine. For a recent discussion of this,see Seán Duffy, "Ostmen, Irish, and Welsh
2 CONC  in the Eleventh Century",Peritia 9 (1995), 378-96.]
2 CONT
2 CONT 18. Owain ab Edwin, d. 1104 [AC.b 1104: "Owinus filius Edwinus obiit."],Welsh chieftan in Tegeingl. [ABT.2b,e,5a]
