2 CONT 65-67. Unknown.
2 CONT
2 CONT 68. Sitric mac Amlaíb (Old Norse Sigtryggr Silkiskeggi), king of Dublin,deposed 1036, d. 1042 [AU].
2 CONT
2 CONT 69. Slani ingen Briain [GaC] [See note under #17. The fact that Sitricwas married to a daughter of Brian is also confirmed by the early twelfthcentury source Cogadh Gaedhel re Gallaibh ("War of the Gaedhil with theGaill"), ed. J. 
2 CONC H. Todd (Rolls Series 48, London, 1867), pp. 193, 257.]
2 CONT
2 CONT 70. Dúnlaing mac Tuathail (of the Uí Muiredaig branch of Uí Dúnlaing),king of Laigin d. 1014 [AU] [GaC]
2 CONT
2 CONT 71. Unknown.
2 CONT
2 CONT 72. Unknown [See note under #36]
2 CONT
2 CONT 73. Unknown.
2 CONT
2 CONT 74. Cynfyn ap Gwerstan (same as #48)
2 CONT
2 CONT 75. Unknown [Note: ByT, p. 101 explicitly states that Iwerydd ferchCynfyn (#37) was Cynfyn's daughter by a mother (unnamed) different fromAngharad. ABT.2f,7k states that Angharad was Iweydd's mother. Since it isa common mistake to
2 CONC  assume that all of a man's children are by his knownwife, it is more likely that ByT is correct here. For Angharad and herancestors, see #49, #98, etc.]
2 CONT
2 CONT 76-95. Unknown
2 CONT
2 CONT 96. Gwerystan [EWGT] [Note: Since his name appears in ByT, p. 101 as apatronymic for Cynfyn, I am inclined to view the name as correct, but theearlier generations of his pedigree show wide variation, and are probablya late inventi
2 CONC on.]
2 CONT
2 CONT 97. Unknown [Note: Late sources make her Nest, daughter of Cadell apBrochwel, king of Powys, which is chronologically impossible.]
2 CONT
2 CONT 98. Maredudd ap Owain, d. 999 [AC] [ABT.1e,7j,k]
2 CONT
2 CONT 99-127. Unknown
2 CONT
2 CONT Generation 8
2 CONT
2 CONT 128. Meuric ab Idwal Voel, d. 986 [AC]. [JC.25; see also DNB 10, 412]
2 CONT
2 CONT 129-135. Unknown.
2 CONT
2 CONT 136. Amlaíb Cuaran (Old Norse Óláfr Kváran), king of Dublin & York, d.981 [AU] [GaC]
2 CONT
2 CONT 137. Gormlaith ingen Murchada (of Uí Dúnlainge), d. 1030 [AT]. Inaddition to being the wife of Amlaib Cuaran, she was also married to MáelSechnaill mac Domnaill, king of Mide (Meath) and king of Ireland (d.1022), and to Brian Boru
2 CONC ma (#138) [BS 189, 227; R.117c=LL.334c (Rw.14,CGH.13); LL334d (CGH.423)]
2 CONT
2 CONT 138. Brian Bóruma mac Cennétig (of Dál Cais), king of Mumu (Munster) andIreland, killed 23 Apr 1014 after his forces had been victorious at theBattle of Clontarf [AU] [GaC; R.152b=LL.322f (Rw.1278, CGH.237);R.154a=LL.336d=Lec.225R
2 CONC b (Rw.1359, CGH.250)]
2 CONT
2 CONT 139. Unknown. [Brian had four known wives, and no known source stateswhich wife was Slani's mother.]
2 CONT
2 CONT 140. Tuathal mac Augaire (of the Uí Muiredaig branch of Uí Dúnlainge,ancestor of the family of Ua Tuathail, i.e., O'Toole), king of Laigin, d.958 [AU] [R.117c=LL.337d=BB.138a (Rw.11, CGH.12)]
2 CONT
2 CONT 141-195. Unknown or duplicated.
2 CONT
2 CONT 196. Owain ap Hywel Dda, king of South Wales, d. 988 [AC] [HG.1,2, wherehe appears as "[O]uen map [H]iguel" in the former (which gives hisancestry through his father), and "[O]uein map Elen" in the latter (whichgives his ancestry 
2 CONC through his mother). The letters in brackets areaccidental omissions. Since the early forms of the names in HG are somuch different from the modern Welsh forms, they will be given for eachof Owain's ancestors as they appear in HG 
2 CONC for sake of comparison.]
2 CONT
2 CONT 197. Unknown. [The claim that she was Angharad ferch Llywelyn ap Merfynap Rhodri (see #1024) appears only in late manuscripts, and should beregarded as dubious. See EWGT, p. 141.]
2 CONT
2 CONT 198-255. Unknown.
2 CONT
2 CONT Generation 9
2 CONT
2 CONT 256. Idwal Voel ab Anarawd, d. 943 [AC], king of Gwynedd. [JC.25; seealso DNB.10.412]
2 CONT
2 CONT 257. Unknown. [Note: Lewys Dwnn's visitation (LD.ii.100) gives Idwal'swife as Mereddon ferch Cadwr, but this late source cannot be trusted forsuch an early marriage.]
2 CONT
2 CONT 258-271. Unknown
2 CONT
2 CONT 272. Sitric ua Ímair (Old Norse Sigtryggr), king of Dublin and York, d.927 [AU].
2 CONT
2 CONT 273. Unknown. [Note: Sitric married a sister of Æthelstan of England in926, but it is not chronologically feasible for her to be the mother ofAmlaib Cuaran.]
2 CONT
2 CONT 274. Murchad mac Finn (of the Uí Fáeláin branch of Uí Dúnlainge), king ofLaigin, d. 972 [AU] [R.117c=LL334c (Rw.13, CGH.13); R.117d=BB.138a(Rw.18, CGH.14); LL337f (CGH.423)]
2 CONT
2 CONT 275. Unknown.
2 CONT
2 CONT 276. Cennétig mac Lorcain (of Dál Cais), king of Thomond, d. 951 [AU][R.152b=LL.322f (Rw.1277-8, CGH.237); R.154a=LL.336d=Lec.225Rb (Rw.1359,CGH.250)]
2 CONT
2 CONT 277. Be Bind ingen Aurchada (of Uí Briúin Seóla). [BS.188, 227, 314, 338]
2 CONT
2 CONT 278-279. Unknown.
2 CONT
2 CONT 280. Augaire mac Ailella (of the Uí Muiredaig branch of Uí Dúnlainge),king of Laigin, d. 917, having been killed in the Battle of Cennfuait bySitric ua Imair (#272) [AU] [R.117c=LL.337d=BB.138a (Rw.11, CGH.12)]
2 CONT
2 CONT 281-391. Unknown or duplicated.
2 CONT
2 CONT 392. Hywel Dda ap Cadell, king of South Wales, d. 950 [AC]. [HG.1:"[H]iguel map Catell"]
2 CONT
2 CONT 393. Elen ferch Llywarch, d. 929 [AC.b: "Helena obiit"] [HG.2: "Elen mercIoumarc" (a mistake for "Loumarc")]
2 CONT
2 CONT 394-511. Unknown.
2 CONT
2 CONT Generation 10
2 CONT 512. Anarawd ap Rhodri Mawr, d. 916 [AU, AC], king of Gwynedd. [JC.25;see also DNB.10.412]
2 CONT
2 CONT 513-543. Unknown.
2 CONT
2 CONT 544. NN mac Ímair (first name unknown, father of Sitric ua Ímair) [Note:Sitric is called a grandson of Ímar (ua Ímair) in the Irish annals, butno satisfactory evidence has been advanced regarding the name of theintervening generat
2 CONC ion. The Irish annals (AU and others) show two sons ofÍmar, Sichfrith (d. 888), and Sitric (d. 896), both of whom appear tohave been kings of Dublin (although the annals do not explicitly givethem that title). Another Dublin king 
2 CONC in the annals, Barid or Barith (d.881), is of unstated parentage in most of the annals, but is referred toas another son of Ímar in CS. of these sons (and possible son), Sitriccan almost certainly be ruled out as the possible fath
2 CONC er of Sitric uaÍmair, because Vikings were very rarely named after their fathers.However, we cannot rule out the possibility that Sitric ua Ímair was theson of another, unknown, son of Ímar.]
2 CONT
2 CONT 545-547. Unknown.
2 CONT
2 CONT 548. Finn mac Máel Mórda (of the Uí Fáeláin branch of Uí Dúnlainge),rígdamna of Laigin, d. 923 [AU] [R.117c=LL334c (Rw.13, CGH.13);R.117d=BB.138a (Rw.18, CGH.14); LL337f (CGH.423)] [Note: There is somedisagreement about the exact 
2 CONC meaning of the term rígdamna. "Prince" or"royal heir" are two possible translations which have been suggested.]
2 CONT
2 CONT 549-551. Unknown.
2 CONT
2 CONT 552. Lorcan mac Lachtnai (of Dál Cais, a sept formerly known as In DéisTuaiscirt, the change in name perhaps occurring about this time, as thename of "Dál Cais" is not documented before the tenth century)[R.152b=LL.322f (Rw.1276-7
2 CONC , CGH.237); R.154a=LL.336d=Lec.225Rb (Rw.1359,CGH.250)]
2 CONT
2 CONT 553. Unknown.
2 CONT
2 CONT 554. Aurchad mac Murchada (of Uí Briúin Seóla), d. 945, king of Uí Briúin[AI] (i.e., probably Uí Briúin Seóla), of Iarthar (West) Connacht, [AU][BS.188,227,314,338; BB.90b]
2 CONT
2 CONT 555. Uncertain. [Royal Irish Academy MS B.IV.2. fo. 52a has a poem whichappears to give two generations of female ancestry of Be Bind ingenAurchada, so more progress on this line is possible in the future. Seethe discussions on th
2 CONC is poem which have taken place insoc.genealogy.medieval for more.]
2 CONT
2 CONT 556-559. Unknown.
2 CONT
2 CONT 560. Ailill mac Dúnlaing, king of Laigin (of the Uí Muiredaig branch ofUí Dúnlainge), d. 871 [AU] [R.117c=LL.337d=BB.138a (Rw.11, CGH.12)]
2 CONT
2 CONT 561-783. Unknown or duplicated.
2 CONT
2 CONT 784. Cadell ap Rhodri, king of South Wales, d. 910 [AC] [HG.1: "Catellmap Rotri"]
2 CONT
2 CONT 785. Unknown.
2 CONT
2 CONT 786. Llywarch ap Hyfaidd, d. 904 [AC] [HG.2: "[L]oumarc map Himeyt" (seecomment under #393)]
2 CONT
2 CONT 787-1023. Unknown.
2 CONT
