1 NOTE {geni:about_me} From Darrell Wolcott 11/25/2017: (please read in EDIT mode to see chart.(Steven Ferry, November 26,2017.)
2 CONT
2 CONT            REVISION NEEDED:
2 CONT
2 CONT            Angharad ferch Dafydd Wynn ap Dafydd, born c. 1360.  She married Dafydd (c. 1350) ap Owain (c. 1320) ap Rhys Goch (c. 1290) ap Rhys (c. 1255) Lord of Marton in Chirbury, Salop.
2 CONT
2 CONT            Dwnn i, 291 cites "Angharad ferch Dafydd Wynn ap Dafydd ap Rhys Llwyd" married "Dafydd ap Owain ap Rhys Goch ap Rhys of Marton.  We believe this Rhys of Marton was a brother of the Dafydd ap Cadwaladr who also appears i
2 CONC n Dwnn i, 291 as "Cadwaladr ap Iorwerth ap Rhys Gwnle ap Rhys Fychan ap Einion ap Gwyn ap Gruffudd".  Bartrum's chart "Gruffudd Chwith" depicts both Rhys of Marton and Dafydd ap Cadwaladr without connecting them as brothers, but c
2 CONC ites two late manuscripts (Llyfr Silin and Cedewain Ms)  which claim that Rhys Gwnle ferch Rhys Fychan was "ap Dafydd ap Gruffudd Chwith descended from Elystan Glodrydd".  We believe the ancestry of these men was correctly given i
2 CONC n Dwnn i, 291 and question the existence of an otherwise unknown "Dafydd ap Gruffudd Chwith" in the families descended from Elystan Glodrydd (or from anyone else).
2 CONT
2 CONT FURTHER DATA:
2 CONT
2 CONT         The Dwnn pedigree was actually that of Pryce of Gunley, a family descended from Einion ap Seisyllt.  It depicted Hugh ap Watkin ap Ieuan ap Ieuan (of Einion's descendants) as being the son of Lleuci ferch Dafydd ap Owain a
2 CONC p Rhys Goch ap Rhys of Marton, and the mother of Lleuci as Angharad ferch Dafydd Wynn ap Dafydd ap Rhys Llwyd, and the mother of Angharad as Myfanwy ferch Dafydd ap Einion ap Ednyfed ap Sulien.
2 CONT
2 CONT          The pedigree also says that the mother of Watkin ap Ieuan was Ales ferch Gruffudd ap Maredudd ap Dafydd ap Cadwaladr ap Iorwerth ap Rhys Gwnle ap Rhys Fychan ap Einion ap Gwyn ap Gruffudd.  Thus:
2 CONT
2 CONT                              1015  Gruffudd II (a)
2 CONT                                            l
2 CONT                               1050  Gwyn II
2 CONT                                            l
2 CONT                               1085  Einion
2 CONT                                            l
2 CONT                           1120  Rhys Fychan
2 CONT                                            l
2 CONT                            1150  Rhys Gwnle
2 CONT                                            l
2 CONT                             1185  Iorwerth
2 CONT                                            l
2 CONT                            1220  Cadwaladr
2 CONT                        ___________l____________
2 CONT                        l                                        l
2 CONT          1255  Rhys of Marton          1250  Dafydd
2 CONT                       l                                         l
2 CONT       1290  Rhys Fychan              1280  Maredudd         to Einion ap Seisyllt
2 CONT                       l                                         l                              l
2 CONT          1320  Owain                      1315  Gruffudd            1310  Ieuan
2 CONT                       l                                         l                              l
2 CONT          1350  Dafydd (b)                   1350  Ales============Ieuan  1340
2 CONT                       l                                                      l
2 CONT          1385  Lleuci=======================Watkin  1370
2 CONT
2 CONT            (a)  ap Beli II ap Selyf II ap Brochwel II of the Powys Royal Family
2 CONT            (b)  This Dafydd married Angharad ferch Dafydd Wynn; her mother was Myfanwy ferch Dafydd ap Einion.
2 CONT             The link shown in red is NOT made in the pedigree but I suggest it is correct, with the elder brother, Dafydd, remaining at Gunley and the younger brother relocating to Marton.  Clearly both families were close to the 
2 CONC family shown in the far right column
2 CONT
2 CONT Please see Peter Bartrum: Gruffudd Chwith; https://www.geni.com/documents/view?doc_id=6000000173393042830 [NOTE: Bartrum charts Gruffudd Chwith as descending from Elystan Glodrydd, but he is nowhere located in the Elystan Glodrydd
2 CONC  charts. His descendants listed after son Dafydd are more properly charted as deriving from Rhys Fychan ap Einion (Rhys Fychan ab Einion). Please see notes on that profile covering this line as charted by Wolcott] (Steven Ferry, S
2 CONC eptember 20, 2023.)
