2 CONT =William III de Braose (or Briouse or Briouze), 4th Lord of Bramber=
2 CONT
2 CONT http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/ENGLISHNOBILITYMEDIEVAL3.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT '''WILLIAM [III] de Briouse''', son of '''WILLIAM [II] de Briouse Lord of Abergavenny, Briouse, Bramber, Brecon and Over-Gwent & his wife Berthe of Hereford''' (-Corbeil 9 Apr 1211, bur Paris, Saint-Victor).  
2 CONT
2 CONT * A manuscript which narrates the descents of the founders of Lanthony Abbey names “Willielmus, Egidius et Reginaldus” as the three sons of “Willelmo Brewes” and his wife “Berta…comitis Milonis secunda filia”, adding that William 
2 CONC was disinherited by King John[1184].  
2 CONT * The Red Book of the Exchequer refers to "Willelmus de Breose xxviii l de honore de Berdestaple" in Devonshire in [1186/87][1185].  
2 CONT * The Red Book of the Exchequer, listing scutage payments in [1190/91], records "Willelmus de Braosa" in Sussex[1186].  The Red Book of the Exchequer, listing scutage payments in [1194/95], names "Willelmus de Breose" among those 
2 CONC granted delay in payment "per brevis" in Buckinghamshire, Bedfordshire[1187].  
2 CONT * "Willelmus de Braiosa, Philippi filius" notified "filio suo" that he had donated "Armigetone mansionem" to the monks of Saint-Florent by charter dated to [1140], witnessed by "Robertus frater meus…", later confirmed by "Willelmu
2 CONC s dominus de Braiosa filius Philippi, avi mei filii Willelmi" witnessed by "Bertam conjugem meam, Philippum fratrem meum…"[1188].  
2 CONT * King John confirmed "honore de Limeric" to "Willo de Braos", as King Henry II had granted it to "Philipp de Braos avunculo predicti Willlemi", by charter dated 12 Jan 1201[1189].  
2 CONT * "Willelmus de Braosa dominus de Brechen" donated property to Flaxley Abbey, Gloucestershire, for the souls of "uxoris meæ Matildis de Sancto Walerico et puerorum nostrorum", by undated charter, witnessed by "Willelmo et Philippo
2 CONC  filiis meis"[1190].  
2 CONT * His lands were forfeited by King John in 1208[1191].  
2 CONT * The 13th century Histoire des ducs de Normandie et des rois d´Angleterre records that "Guillaumes de Brayouse" fled from King John to France[1192].  
2 CONT * The Annals of Waverley record that “Willelmus…de Brausa” fled “apud Sorham” after his wife and son were captured and died in Paris soon afterwards[1193].  
2 CONT * The Annals of Margan record the death in 1211 of “Willielmus de Breusa senior exul in Francia”[1194].
2 CONT
2 CONT m ([1170/75]) '''MATHILDE de Saint-Valéry''', daughter of BERNARD de Saint-Valéry & his [second wife Anora ---] (-Corfe Castle 1210).  
2 CONT * The 13th century Histoire des ducs de Normandie et des rois d´Angleterre names "fille fu Bernart de Saint-Waleri…Mehaus" as the wife of "Guillaumes de Brayouse", commenting that she once boasted about her cows to "Bauduin le con
2 CONC te d´Aubemalle son neveu"[1195].   
2 CONT * A manuscript which narrates the descents of the founders of Lanthony Abbey names “Matildis de S. Walerico, quondam uxoris Willielmi de Brewes” when recording the marriage of her daughter[1196].   
2 CONT * "Willelmus de Braosa dominus de Brechen" donated property to Flaxley Abbey, Gloucestershire, for the souls of "uxoris meæ Matildis de Sancto Walerico et puerorum nostrorum", by undated charter, witnessed by "Willelmo et Philippo
2 CONC  filiis meis"[1197].   
2 CONT * The Annals of Waverley record that “Matildis matrona nobilis cognomento de la Haie, uxor Willelmi de Braose” was captured with “Willelmo filio suo milite…in Galwaitha” in 1210 and starved to death “apud Windeshores”[1198].   
2 CONT * A manuscript which narrates the descents of the founders of Lanthony Abbey records that “Mathildis uxor eius et Willielmus filius eorum” (referring to William, son of “Willelmo Brewes” and his wife “Berta…comitis Milonis secunda
2 CONC  filia”) were imprisoned by King John and died in prison[1199].   
2 CONT * The Annals of Dunstable record that “Willelmum de Brause juniorem et sororem eius et Matildam matrem eius” were captured in Ireland in 1210 by King John, adding that they later died in prison[1200].   
2 CONT * The 13th century Histoire des ducs de Normandie et des rois d´Angleterre records that "Mehaus sa feme [Guillaumes de Braiouse] et Guillaumes ses fils" fled from King John to Ireland where they were captured at "le castiel de Cra
2 CONC cfergu", taken to England, and imprisoned at "el castiel del Corf" where they were starved to death[1201].   
2 CONT * The question whether "Mathilde de Saint-Valéry" and "Mathilde de la Haie" refer to the same person appears to be resolved by the 13th century Histoire des ducs de Normandie et des rois d´Angleterre which records her parentage an
2 CONC d the circumstances of her death in the same lengthy passage. 
2 CONT
2 CONT William & his wife had nine children: 
2 CONT
2 CONT 1.         '''MARGERY''' ([1175/85]-after 1255). ... may have been her mother´s daughter by an earlier marriage, not the daughter of William de Briouse, although no other primary source has yet been identified which suggests that 
2 CONC Maud married twice.   m WALTER de Lacy Lord of Meath, son of HUGH de Lacy Lord of Meath & his first wife Rose de Monmouth ([1172]-before 24 Feb 1241). 
2 CONT
2 CONT 2.         '''LAURETTE''' (-Hackington 4 Mar [1266 or after]).  ...  m ROBERT de Breteuil "FitzPernel" Earl of Leicester, son of ROBERT de Beaumont Earl of Leicester & his wife Pernelle de Grantmesnil (-20/21 Oct 1204, bur Leicest
2 CONC er Abbey). 
2 CONT
2 CONT 3.        ''' ELEANOR''' [Annor] (-after 26 Jan 1241).  ...  m (before 1210) HUGH de Mortimer of Wigmore, son of ROGER de Mortimer & his wife Isabel de Ferrers (-10 Nov 1227, bur Wigmore). 
2 CONT
2 CONT 4.         '''WILLIAM [IV] de Briouse''' (-Corfe 1210).  ... m as her first husband, MATILDA [Joan] de Clare, daughter of RICHARD de Clare Earl of Hertford & his wife Amicie of Gloucester ([1185/90]-).  
2 CONT
2 CONT 5.         '''PHILIP de Briouse''' .  ... m as her first husband, MATILDA de Pont de l´Arche, daughter of --- (-after 1 Sep 1227).  ...
2 CONT
2 CONT 6.         '''MATILDA de Briouse''' . ... m (1189) GRUFFYDD ap Rhys, son of RHYS ap Gruffydd King of Deheubarth & his wife Gwenllian of Powys (-[Jul/Aug] 1201).  He succeeded his father in 1197 as King of Deheubarth. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 7.         daughter .  The Annals of Dunstable record that “Willelmum de Brause juniorem et sororem eius et Matildam matrem eius” were captured in Ireland in 1210 by King John, adding that they later died in prison[615]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 8.         --- .  The identity of Lucy´s parents is not known.  Her father or mother may have been one of the other children of William [III] de Briouse who are named in this section.  m <nowiki>----</nowiki>  One child: 
2 CONT
2 CONT >a)         LEUCA (-before 28 Aug 1236).  ...  m GEOFFREY de Canville, son of --- (-before 20 Sep 1219). 
2 CONT
2 CONT 9.         '''REYNOLD de Briouse''' (-[5 May 1227/9 Jun 1228]).  ... m firstly GRECIA, daughter of WILLIAM Briwere & his wife Beatrix de Vaux.  ... m secondly ([1215/16]) GWLADUS Ddu, illegitimate daughter of LLEWELYN ap Iorwerth 
2 CONC Prince of North Wales & his mistress --- (-Windsor 1251).  ... 
2 CONT
