2 CONC tinct or Dormant, new ed., 13 volumes in 14 (1910-1959; reprint in 6 volumes, Gloucester, U.K.: Alan Sutton Publishing, 2000), volume I, page 22. Hereinafter cited as The Complete Peerage.
2 CONT
2 CONT William de Braose, 7th Baron Abergavenny and 4th Lord of Bramber (1144/1153 – August 9, 1211), court favourite of King John, at the peak of his power was also Lord of Gower, Abergavenny, Brecknock, Builth, Radnor, Kington, Limeric
2 CONC k, Glamorgan,Skenfrith, Briouze in Normandy, Grosmont, and White Castle.
2 CONT
