2 CONT # Death: Aft 5 Feb 1227-1228 in England 1 2 1 3 3 4 2
2 CONT # Change Date: 21 Sep 2005 at 15:22
2 CONT '''Note''': He [William de Ferrieres] married Sibyl, daughter of William de Braiose, Lord of Bramber, by Bertha (heiress of Brecon and Over Gwent), sister and coheir of William DE HEREFORD, and 2nd daughter of Miles (DE GLOUCESTER
2 CONC ),EARL OF HEREFORD. He died on Crusade, at the siege of Acre, in palestine, in 1190, before 21 October. His wife survived him, and married 2ndly Adamde Port, Lord of Basing, who died 1213, and was, perhaps, living as late as 5 Feb
2 CONC ruary 1227/8. [Complete Peerage IV:192-4, XIV:250, (transcribed by Dave Utzinger)]
2 CONT
2 CONT Father: William De Braiose b: 1112 in Abergavenny, Over Gwent, Monmouthshire, Wales
2 CONT Mother: Bertha FitzPWalter, de Piers, de Gloucester b: Abt 1110-1130 in Gloucester, Gloucestershire, England
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage 1: William "Walkelin" (Walchaline) de Ferrers b: Abt 1135-1140 in Ferriers-Saint-Hilaire, France
2 CONT Married: 1173-1174 in of Sussex, England
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage 2: Sybil De Braose b: 1146-1150 in Bramber, Sussex, England
2 CONT Married: 1173-1174 in of Sussex, England
2 CONT
2 CONT >Children
2 CONT >1. Has Children William II De Ferrers b: Abt 1162-1170 in Ferrers, Derbyshire, England
2 CONT >2. Has Children Agatha de Ferrers b: 1168-1172 in Chartley, Staffordshire, England
2 CONT >3. Has Children Petronilla De Ferrers b: Abt 1170
2 CONT >4. Has No Children Henry de Ferrers b: 1176
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Source''': Abbrev: Susan Cary – Title: Susan Cary 
2 CONT ----
2 CONT >"21. Another example of this custom may be seen in the daughter of an earlier Braose family. '''Sybil de Braose''' married, first, William de Ferrers, Earl of Derby, and, second, Adam de Port. After the death of Adam de Port, Syb
2 CONC il was known as the Countess of Ferrers. (See NCP 11:321)"
2 CONT >'''Source''': Aubrey Stratton, Eugene. 1988. ' Applied Genealogy,'' [https://www.google.com/books/edition/Applied_Genealogy/HaBpAAAAMAAJ?hl=en&gbpv=1&bsq=%22Sybil+de+Braose%22&dq=%22Sybil+de+Braose%22&printsec=frontcover '''p. 28
2 CONC 1.''']
2 CONT
2 CONT >>"William de Ferrers, Earl of Derby – born about 1130 at Tutbury Castle, Derbyshire, England; married about 1173/74 in Sussex, England to '''Sybil de Braose''' (born about 1157 in Bramber, Sussex, England), daughter of William de
2 CONC  Braose, Sheriff (1114-1192) and Bertha de Gloucester (born about 1130); died before 21 Oct 1190 at Siege of Acre, Jerusalem; children: William, Agatha, Millicent, Robert, Elizabeth."
2 CONT >>'''Source''': ''Historical Genealogy Magazine'', Volume 4. Philadelphia, PA: CharDan Publishing. [https://www.google.com/books/edition/Historical_Genealogy_Magazine/Pm5bAAAAMAAJ?hl=en&gbpv=1&bsq=%22Sybil+de+Braose%22&dq=%22Sybil
2 CONC +de+Braose%22&printsec=frontcover '''p. 21.''']
2 CONT
2 CONT >"Robert instead of William, in a grant quoted to ''Discoverie of Errours'', by Vincent in which '''''Sybilla de Braose''''' is give as the name of the donor's wife and the mother of his son William. That son, in a confirmation to
2 CONC  the monastery of Tutbury lists his ancestors as follows:—Henricus de Ferrariis fundator huiusdem..."
2 CONT >'''Source''': Leicestershire Archaeological Society. ''Transactions'', Vols .20-21, [https://www.google.com/books/edition/Transactions/y9UxAQAAIAAJ?hl=en&gbpv=1&bsq=%22Sybilla+de+Braose%22&dq=%22Sybilla+de+Braose%22&printsec=fron
2 CONC tcover '''p. 160.''']
2 CONT
