1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/enguntdk.htm#_Toc21080974
2 CONT
2 CONT HERBERT FitzHerbert [II], son of HERBERT FitzHerbert [I] & his wife Sibyl Corbet ([1125/35]-before 18 Jul 1204).   m LUCY of Hereford, daughter of MILES of Gloucester Earl of Hereford & his wife Sibylle de Neufmarché (before 1143-
2 CONC [1219/20] or after, bur Lanthony Priory, Gloucester). 
2 CONT
2 CONT Herbert & his wife had two [SIC: thee]  children: 
2 CONT *1.         REYNOLD FitzHerbert (-[1190/92]).  The primary source which confirms his parentage has not yet been identified.  
2 CONT *2.         PIERS FitzHerbert of Blaenllyfni (-1 Jul 1235, bur Reading).
2 CONT *3.         MATTHEW FitzHerbert (-[13 Jun 1230/Feb 1231]).  The Red Book of the Exchequer records "Mathaeus filius Herberti" holding one knight’s fee "Stoke" in Wiltshire, and one in Devonshire from "honor Gloucestriæ", in [1210/1
2 CONC 2][616].  A letter of Henry III King of England to the bishop of Rochester, dated 13 Jun 1230, appointing him to make an assize of arms in Kent, names "Petrus filius Hereberti…Matthæus filius Hereberti" as those charged with a sim
2 CONC ilar exercise in Berkshire and Wiltshire respectively[617].  Matthew, his wife and descendants are shown by Eyton but the primary sources which confirm the information have not yet been identified[618].  m (before Jun 1200) JOAN P
2 CONC atric, daughter of --- & his wife Mabel Patric[619] (-after 21 Feb 1231).  Bracton records a claim, dated 1219, by "Robertus filius Briani, Oliuerus Auenel, Gaufridus Talebot et Adam de Dornapetona" against "Matheum filium Hereber
2 CONC ti et Johannam uxorem eius"[620]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Matthew & his wife had three children: 
2 CONT *a)         HERBERT FitzMatthew (-3 or 5 Feb 1245).  "Herbert son of Matthew" was granted "the manor of Warblinton, late of Robert de Curcy" dated 10 Jun 1231[621].  "Herbert son of Matthew" was granted "a weekly market…at Emelesw
2 CONC urth…" dated 20 Apr 1239[622].  m MILLICENT Paynell, daughter of WILLIAM Paynell of Bampton, Devon & his wife Alice Briwere (-before 1249).  The Complete Peerage states that Herbert FitzMatthew married “Milicent da. and coh. of Wi
2 CONC lliam Paynel of Bampton, Devon” but does not cite the corresponding primary source[623].  An indication of the connection between the two families is provided by the order dated 4 Feb 1228 under which Henry III King of England gra
2 CONC nted "custodiam terre et heredis Willelmi Paynel" to "Hereberto filio Mathey" and ordered the sheriff of Devon to release them to him[624].  She must have died childless before 1249 when an inquisitions after her brother’s death n
2 CONC ame his sister Aude as his heir. 
2 CONT *b)         PETER FitzMatthew (-1255).  Land recovered from "Peter son of Matthew" was regranted dated 18 Aug 1252[625]. 
2 CONT *c)         JOHN FitzMatthew (-before 19 Jan 1261).  A debt of "Peter son of Matthew" was granted, to be received from "John son of Matthew brother and heir of the said Peter son of Matthew" dated 28 Dec 1256[626].  m[627] as her 
2 CONC first husband, MARGARET de Berkeley, daughter of THOMAS de Berkeley of Berkeley, Gloucestershire & his wife Joan [de Somery].  She married secondly (before 18 Oct 1265) Ansel Basset of Winford and Saltford, Somerset.  John & his w
2 CONC ife had one child: 
