2 CONC to Saint Olaf II of Norway. After the Norman Conquest the church came into the possession of the Anglo-Breton magnate Alan Rufus who granted the lands to Abbot Stephen and a group of monks from Whitby. The abbey church was refound
2 CONC ed in 1088[1][3] when the King, William Rufus, visited York in January or February of that year[4] and gave the monks additional lands.  ....
