2 CONT
2 CONT Born: Abt 1110, Penthievre, Morbihan, Bretagne, France  
2 CONT Married (1): 1st husband 
2 CONT Married (2): Before 1162, 2nd husband 1st wife
2 CONT Died: Before 1187  Another name for Olive was Olive de PENTHIEVRE.   
2 CONT
2 CONT General Notes: William [de St. John] married, 1stly, in or after 1150 and before 1162, Olive, daughter of COUNT STEPHEN OF BRITTANY, LORD OF RICHMOND, and widow of Henry DE FOUGÈRES; and 2ndly, Godeheut, whose parentage is unknown
2 CONC . He died s.p. between Michaelmas 1201 and Michaelmas 1202, and was succeeded by his great-nephew William DE PORT, afterwards William DE ST. JOHN. [Complete Peerage XI;343-4, transcribed by Dave Utzinger)]   
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage Information: Olive married Seigneur Henry DE FOUGERES, son of Seigneur Raoul I DE FOUGERES and Avoise (Havoise) DE BRIONNE, in 1st husband. (Seigneur Henry DE FOUGERES was born about 1095 in Fougeres, Ille-et-Vilaine, Bre
2 CONC tagne, France and died in 1154.) 
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage Information: Olive also married William de ST. JOHN of Halnaker before 1162 in 2nd husband 1st wife . (William de ST. JOHN of Halnaker was born about 1117 in St-Jean-le-Thomas, Manche, Normandy, France and died about 1189
2 CONC  in Halnaker, Sussex, England (dsp).)
