1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ====FMG: Brittany – [https://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/brittcope.htm#HenriBretagnedied1183A Cornouaille, Penthievre]
2 CONT * 3. '''HENRI de Penthièvre''' ([1100]-early 1183). The undated record of an enquiry relating to the property rights of Henri d’Avaugour states that "le comte Estienne" had three children “Geffroi, Alain et Henri aieul de cest Hen
2 CONC ri ci-dessus”, adding that Henri remained with his father and succeeded him “aux terres de Treguer et Guengamp”, was expelled “après la mort du comte Alain” by “son fils Conan...à l’aide du vicomte de Rohan”, but later recovered h
2 CONC is territories[443]. “Stephanus comes Britannie Eudonis comitis filius” notified King Henry I and “omnibus filiis suis G[aufrido] videlicet atque Alano necnon et Henrico omnibusque hominibus suis Francie et Anglis” of his donation
2 CONC  to Bury St. Edmunds abbey, by charter dated 1135 [see above for full extract][444]. He succeeded his father in [1135/36] as Comte de Tréguier et de Guingamp. "Alan comes et indigena of England and count of Brittany" donated prope
2 CONC rty to the abbey of Holy Trinity, Sauvigny by charter dated to [1137/46], subscribed by "…Hainrico fratre meo…"[445]. — [https://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/brittcope.htm#HenriBretagnedied1183A '''see below'''].
2 CONT
2 CONT -https://fr.wikipedia.org/wiki/Henri_de_Tr%C3%A9gor
