2 CONT --------------------------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Tudor, son of Gronw, who lived to be called Tudor Hen or the old Tudor, founded the Carmelite friary in Bangor and was grandfather of Tudor Vychan ap Gronw of Trecastell, who is said to have assumed the style of a knight, and to h
2 CONC ave had that rank confirmed to him by Edward III.
2 CONT
2 CONT Goronwy and Morfydd were parents to Tudur Hen, Lord of Penmynydd (d. 1311); Tudur Hen later married Angharad ferch Ithel Fychan, daughter of Ithel Fychan ap Ithel Gan, Lord of Englefield. They were parents to Goronwy ap Tudur, Lor
2 CONC d of Penmynydd (d. 1331)
2 CONT
2 CONT Tudor ap Grono of Penmynedd1
2 CONT
2 CONT Father	Lord of Tref-Gastel Grono ap Ednyfed Vychan1
2 CONT
2 CONT Mother	Morfydd verch Meuric o Gwent1
2 CONT
2 CONT      Tudor ap Grono of Penmynedd was the son of Lord of Tref-Gastel Grono ap Ednyfed Vychan and Morfydd verch Meuric o Gwent.1
2 CONT
