1 NOTE {geni:about_me} William FitzRaymond le Gras, the eldest son of Raymond le Gros FitzWilliam, who granted a charter to his burgesses of Sodbury, before 1190; and, assuming the habit of St. Augustine, became prior of Christ Church, D
2 CONC ublin, and died, 1212. (He is listed as William Sr., Willielmus Primogenitus" and has a younger brother William, listed as William Jr., who became Raymond FitzWilliam's heir and oldest son).
2 CONT
2 CONT source: www.libraryireland.com/Pedigrees2/redmond-1.php
