2 CONT Maurice fitz Thomas1 M, #155621, b. circa 1197, d. before 1253 Last Edited=4 Jan 2009
2 CONT      Maurice fitz Thomas was born circa 1197.2 He was the son of Thomas fitz Maurice and Ellinor de Marisec.1 He died before 1253.1
2 CONT      Circa 1213 he was a hostage in England.2 In 1215 he was sent back to Ireland in charge of the Justiciar, Geoffrey Marsh.2 Citations
2 CONT
2 CONT     [S6] G.E. Cokayne; with Vicary Gibbs, H.A. Doubleday, Geoffrey H. White, Duncan Warrand and Lord Howard de Walden, editors, The Complete Peerage of England, Scotland, Ireland, Great Britain and the United Kingdom, Extant, Exti
2 CONC nct or Dormant, new ed., 13 volumes in 14 (1910-1959; reprint in 6 volumes, Gloucester, U.K.: Alan Sutton Publishing, 2000), volume VII, page 200. Hereinafter cited as The Complete Peerage.
