1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/WALES.htm#Llywellyndied1240B
2 CONT
2 CONT attributed to mistresses 2-7; married William de Lacy, son of Hugh de Lacy and his second wife Rosa.
2 CONT
2 CONT Janet Palo-Jackson, volunteer curator.
2 CONT
2 CONT This profile is discussional.
2 CONT
2 CONT See papers by E. G. Lloyd on "Who was Gwenllian de Lacy?" in Arch. Cambrensis (July, 1919):
2 CONT
2 CONT "William 'Gorm'" married this daughter of Llewellyn the Great but left no issue by her.
2 CONT
2 CONT Also see "A history of Medieval Ireland from 1086 to 1513" by Edmund Curtis, p. 135:
2 CONT
2 CONT "The annals of Ulster record in 1233 the death of William de Lacy. His welsh wife Gwenllian survived him and returned to Wales, but they left no issue".
2 CONT
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Llewelyn_the_Great
2 CONT
2 CONT Issue
2 CONT
2 CONT Dafydd ap Llywelyn
2 CONT
2 CONT  Gruffydd ap Llywelyn
2 CONT
2 CONT  Elen ferch Llywelyn
2 CONT
2 CONT  Gwladus Ddu
2 CONT
2 CONT  Marared ferch Llywelyn
2 CONT
2 CONT ============ Gwenllian ferch Llywelyn
2 CONT
2 CONT  Angharad ferch Llywelyn
2 CONT
2 CONT  Susanna ferch Llywelyn
2 CONT
2 CONT According to represented data "William 'Gorm'" and Gwenllian, daughter of Llewellyn, had no mutual children. This is fact from independent sources.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/IRELAND.htm#WilliamLacyMdauLlywelyn
2 CONT
2 CONT In his report to King Henry dated 5 Aug 1224 following the capture of castle Trum, William Marshall Earl of Pembroke records that "the wife of William de Lascy, the daughter of Llewllyn, Griffin´s sister, the wife of Thomas Blund,
2 CONC  William´s brother, and the mother of William, of Thomas, and of him that was killed" were in the castle[866]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ==== There is the mistake: not the daughter of Llewellyn (who survived her husband William de Lacy), but the elder sister of Llevellyn!!!
2 CONT
2 CONT ---
2 CONT
2 CONT Record in "The Legacy of the de Lacy, Lacey, Lacy Family 1066-1994", p. 56: 
2 CONT
2 CONT "He did miss his association with his half-brother William de Lacy. William
2 CONT
2 CONT ==== married the elder sister!!! of Llewellyn,
2 CONT
2 CONT the rebellious Prince of Wales, and William's activities absorbed in Leinster and Limerick...
2 CONT
2 CONT ==== William married Gwenllian or Gwendoline, or Winnefred as she variously called.
2 CONT
2 CONT ==== Gwellian was sister!!! to Llewellyn, the paramount Prince of Wales,
2 CONT
2 CONT who kept wales in open rebellion to British rule for two generations".
2 CONT
2 CONT See also:
2 CONT ==== De Lacy-Bellingari, Edward de Lacy-Harnett, The roll of the house of Lacy : pedigrees, military memoirs and synoptical history of the ancient and illustrious family of De Lacy from the earliest times, in all its branches, to 
2 CONC the present day.
2 CONT
2 CONT See papers by E. G. Lloyd on "Who was Gwenllian de Lacy?" in Arch. Cambrensis (July, 1919):
2 CONT
2 CONT "William 'Gorm'" married this daughter of Llewellyn the Great but left no issue by her.
2 CONT
2 CONT Also see "A history of Medieval Ireland from 1086 to 1513" by Edmund Curtis, p. 135:
2 CONT
2 CONT "The annals of Ulster record in 1233 the death of William de Lacy. His welsh wife Gwenllian survived him and returned to Wales, but they left no issue".
2 CONT
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Llewelyn_the_Great
2 CONT
2 CONT Issue
2 CONT
2 CONT Dafydd ap Llywelyn
2 CONT
2 CONT  Gruffydd ap Llywelyn
2 CONT
2 CONT  Elen ferch Llywelyn
2 CONT
2 CONT  Gwladus Ddu
2 CONT
2 CONT  Marared ferch Llywelyn
2 CONT
2 CONT ============ Gwenllian ferch Llywelyn
2 CONT
2 CONT  Angharad ferch Llywelyn
2 CONT
2 CONT  Susanna ferch Llywelyn
2 CONT
2 CONT According to represented data "William 'Gorm'" and Gwenllian, daughter of Llewellyn, had no mutual clildren. This is fact from independent sources.
