2 CONC .geni.com/documents/view?doc_id=6000000173395392851 [Bartrum charts two "sisters" named Angharad ferch Llewelyn, but dating indicates it could be one woman, married twice] (Steven Ferry, December 29, 2024.)
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ---------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Angharad verch Llewelyn   
2 CONT
2 CONT Angharad was born in May 1205 in Caernarvonshire, Wales.1   Angharad's father was Llewelyn (The Great) ap Iorweth and her mother was Joan Plantagenet.  Her paternal grandparents were Prince of Gwynedd Iowerth Drwyndwn ap Owain and
2 CONC  Marared verch Madog; her maternal grandparents were King of England John (Lackland) Plantagenet of England and Agatha de Ferrers. She had three brothers and three sisters, named Dafydd, Tegwared-Y-Baiswen, Llywelyn, Elen, Margred
2 CONC  and Helen.  She was the oldest of the seven children. She had a half-brother and a half-sister, named Fawr and Ddu.
2 CONT
2 CONT  Lord of Cardigan Philip ap Ivor
2 CONT
2 CONT Philip was born about 1200 in Cardigan, Wales.1   Philip is no longer alive.
2 CONT
2 CONT  Angharad verch Llewelyn
2 CONT
2 CONT Angharad was born in May 1205 in Caernarvonshire, Wales.2 
2 CONT
2 CONT Children
2 CONT
2 CONT   Lord of Cardigan Iscoed ap Philip
2 CONT
2 CONT Iscoed was born about 1225 in Cardigan, Wales.3 
2 CONT
