1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Susanna does not appear in the pedigrees, but in 1228 she was sent to be in the care of Nicholas de Verdon and his wife, the only reference to her in the primary sources.  
2 CONT
2 CONT She is sometimes referred to as a hostage, but the relevant passage, according to Wikipedia says that  ''Henry III King of England granted the upbringing of "L. princeps Norwallie et Johanna uxor sua et…soror nostra Susannam filia
2 CONC m suam" to "Nicholao de Verdun et Clementie uxori sue" by order dated 24 Nov 1228. Her birth date is estimated on the assumption that Susanna was under marriageable age, but older than an infant, at the time.''
2 CONT
2 CONT see  https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Llywelyn_the_Great
2 CONT
2 CONT (December 18, 2015; Anne Brannen, curator)
