1 NOTE {geni:about_me} =Giles de Braose, Bishop of Hereford=
2 CONT
2 CONT GILES de Briouse (-Gloucester 13 Nov 1215, bur Hereford Cathedral).  A manuscript which narrates the descents of the founders of Lanthony Abbey names “Willielmus, Egidius et Reginaldus” as the three sons of “Willelmo Brewes” and h
2 CONC is wife “Berta…comitis Milonis secunda filia”, adding that Giles was Bishop of Hereford[1808].  Giles de Briouse is more often shown in secondary sources as the son of William [III] de Briouse and his wife Mathilde, which is confi
2 CONC rmed as correct by an order dated 10 May 1215 which confirms that "E. Epc Heford" had judgment of the fine made for "terra q fuit W. de Braiosa patris sui"[1809], which must refer to William [III] who died in 1211.  This source al
2 CONC so shows that Giles must have been his parents’ second son, inheriting his father’s lands in preference to the infant son of his deceased older brother William [IV].  Bishop of Hereford 1200.  Matthew Paris records that "Gilo de B
2 CONC rause" was consecrated bishop of Hereford “VIII Kal Oct apud Westmonasterium” in 1200[1810].  The Annals of Dunstable record that “Ægidius Herefordensis episcopus” died in 1216[1811].  
2 CONT
2 CONT http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/ENGLISHNOBILITYMEDIEVAL3.htm#WilliamBriousedied1210A [Revised version]
2 CONT
2 CONT Note: he made Bishop at a remarkably young age - family pull behind that?
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Profile was trash-mash-merged several times, resulting in gibberish.
2 CONT
2 CONT No record of any wife, offspring or extracurricular activity.
2 CONT
2 CONT Variously said to have died at Gloucester, Worcester, or Hereford.
