1 NOTE {geni:about_me} =Laurette de Braose=
2 CONT daughter of William III de Braose and Mathilde de Saint-Valery married Robert de Breteuil Earl of Leicester
2 CONT
2 CONT http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/ENGLISHNOBILITYMEDIEVAL3.htm#_Toc286526791
2 CONT
2 CONT '''LAURETTE''' (-Hackington 4 Mar [1266 or after]).  Her parentage is confirmed by the Testa de Nevill which includes a writ of King John dated 1212 recording that "Willelmus de Brause" granted "manerium de Taustock" in Devon to "
2 CONC comiti Leycestrie in maritagium cum filia sua"[1209].  Robert son of Parnel, Earl of Leicester, donated property to the abbey of Lire for the soul of Loreta his wife, by charter dated to [1190/1204][1210].  She became a recluse at
2 CONC  Hackington, near Canterbury, before Feb 1221[1211].  The necrology of Lyre monastery records the death "4 Mar" of "Laureta comitissa"[1212].  
2 CONT
2 CONT m '''ROBERT de Breteuil "FitzPernel" Earl of Leicester''', son of ROBERT de Beaumont Earl of Leicester & his wife Pernelle de Grantmesnil (-20/21 Oct 1204, bur Leicester Abbey). See http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/ENGLISH%20NOBILI
2 CONC TY%20MEDIEVAL.htm#RobertBeaumontLeicesterdied1204
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT see Wikipedia article: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Loretta_de_Braose,_Countess_of_Leicester
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Primary sources needed. FMG MedLands database does not show this person as a child of John de Braose and Margaret of Wales (verch Llewellyn). 
