1 NOTE {geni:about_me} The only Roger documented in MedLands was a brother, not son, not grandson, of William II de Braose. 
2 CONT * ROGER de Briouse .  “Willielmus de Braosa” confirmed donations to Abergavenny Priory by “Hamelinus de Balon et Brientius comitis filius et Walterus de Herefort et Henricus de Herefort” by undated charter, witnessed by “Rogero fr
2 CONC atre meo…”[1719].  He would have been ''much'' older, though.
2 CONT
2 CONT Since William [III] de Braose and Maud de St. Valery had an indeterminate, though large, number of children, Roger may fit in there also, but would have been at least a third son and in some position that kept him out of the famil
2 CONC y troubles. (A monastery, perhaps? Although being a Bishop didn't stop Giles....)
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT ROGER de Briouse .  “Willielmus de Braosa” confirmed donations to Abergavenny Priory by “Hamelinus de Balon et Brientius comitis filius et Walterus de Herefort et Henricus de Herefort” by undated charter, witnessed by “Rogero frat
2 CONC re meo…”[Dugdale Monasticon IV, Priory of Bergavenny or Abergavenny in Monmouthshire, III, p. 616].  http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/ENGLISHNOBILITYMEDIEVAL3.htm#WilliamBraosedied1192A
