1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Several sources have conflated John de Braose of Knill with his brother, William de Braose.  See Burke's Peerage, p. 589.  (January 2016; Anne Brannen, curator)
2 CONT
2 CONT ******************
2 CONT
2 CONT Primary sources needed. FMG MedLands database does not show this person as a child of John de Braose and Margaret of Wales (verch Llewellyn). However, he is named in Wikipedia and so he will remain on the tree but more documentati
2 CONC on is needed.
2 CONT
2 CONT Secondary sources also include Dugdale's "Baronage," p. 420, according to Hermentrude, writing in  "Notes and Queries," vol. 8, p. 86.  See also "The Magna Charta  Sureties," p. 159.    In both these sources, he is called William.
2 CONC  (December 18, 2015; Anne Brannen, curator)
