1 NOTE {geni:about_me} William de Ferrers, 4th Earl of Derby
2 CONT
2 CONT Links: http://www.celtic-casimir.com/webtree/5/6904.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
2 CONT
2 CONT William II de Ferrers, 4th Earl of Derby, [c.1168–c.1247] was a favourite of King John of England. He succeeded to the estate (but not the title) upon the death of his father at the Siege of Acre in 1190. He was head of a family w
2 CONC hich controlled a large part of Derbyshire which included an area known as Duffield Frith.
2 CONT
2 CONT He adopted his father's allegiance to King Richard as the reigning king. On Richard's return from the Third Crusade, in the company of Earl David Ceannmhor and the Earl of Chester he played a leading role in besieging Nottingham C
2 CONC astle, on the 28th March 1194, which was being held by supporters of John Lackland. For seven weeks after this he held the position of Sheriff of Nottinghamshire and Derbyshire. [1]
2 CONT
2 CONT On the accession of John after the death of his brother, in 1199, William gave him his allegiance, and became a great favourite. He restored to the Ferrars' family the title of Earl of Derby, along with the right to the "third pen
2 CONC ny", and soon afterwards bestowed upon him the manors of Ashbourne and Wirksworth, with the whole of that wapentake, subject to a fee farm rent of £70 per annum. [2]
2 CONT
2 CONT When, in 1213, John surrendered his kingdoms of England and Ireland to the Pope, William was one of the witnesses to the "Bulla Aurea." In the following year William gave surety on behalf of the king for the payment of a yearly tr
2 CONC ibute of 1,000 marks.
2 CONT
2 CONT In the same year, 1214, the King granted the Earl the royal castle of Harestan (Horsley Castle). William was a patron of at least 2 abbeys and 4 priories. In 1216, John made him bailiff of the Peak Forest and warden of the Peak Ca
2 CONC stle Peveril Castle.
2 CONT
2 CONT In that year, John was succeeded by the nine year-old Henry III. Because of continuing discontent about John's violations of the Magna Carta, some of the barons had approached Prince Louis of France who invaded in that year. Willi
2 CONC am Marshal, 1st Earl of Pembroke acting on behalf the young King sought to repel the invaders and pacify the barons. His forces with the assistance of de Ferrers, the Earl of Chester and others, defeated the rebels at the siege of
2 CONC  Lincoln.
2 CONT
2 CONT De Ferrers was allowed to retain the royal castles of Bolsover, Peak and Horston (Horsley until the King's 14th birthday. The last named had been given him in 1215 as a residence for his wife, during its planned absence with the K
2 CONC ing on Crusade. [3] and the Earl was among those who made representation to the King, which would in 1258 led to the Provisions of Oxford .
2 CONT
2 CONT Henry reached his fourteenth birthday in 1222 and his administration sought to recover the three royal castles, to de Ferrers indignation. (In 1254 they would pass to Edward, Henry's son, exacerbating Robert, the sixth's earl's re
2 CONC sentment against the prince.) [4]
2 CONT
2 CONT He was married to Agnes De Kevelioch, sister of Ranulph de Blondeville, 4th Earl of Chester, for 55 years. As the Earl advanced in years he became a martyr to severe attacks of the gout, a disease which terminated his life in the 
2 CONC year 1247. He was succeeded by his elder son, also William, the Fifth Earl of Derby.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children:
2 CONT
2 CONT    1. William de Ferrers, 5th Earl of Derby
2 CONT
2 CONT    2. Sybil de Ferrers, married Sir John Vipont [1], Lord of Appleby and had issue.
2 CONT
2 CONT    3. Sir Thomas of Chartley Ferrers
2 CONT
2 CONT    4. Sir Hugh of Bugbrooke Ferrers (married and had issue)
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT William II was the 4th Earl of Derby.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was 79 years old when he died. 
2 CONT
2 CONT See "My Lines"
2 CONT
2 CONT ( http://homepages.rootsweb.ancestry.com/~cousin/html/p394.htm#i6944 )
2 CONT
2 CONT from Compiler: R. B. Stewart, Evans, GA
2 CONT
2 CONT ( http://homepages.rootsweb.ancestry.com/~cousin/html/index.htm )
2 CONT
