1 OCCU mistress, http://wc.rootsweb.ancestry.com/cgi-bin/igm.cgi?op=GET&db=rwfurtaw&id=I18287
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} >'''ALERT'''
2 CONT >'''1.''' As of 12 Aug 2022, [https://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/ENGLISH%20NOBILITY%20MEDIEVAL1.htm#RobertFerrersdied1225 '''Medilands'''] does ''not'' support this person profile to the attached parentage. 
2 CONT >'''2.''' A [https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Ferrers-286 '''Wikitree'''] profile argues two possible fathers: William vs. Robert. 
2 CONT >'''3.''' Cokayne's volumes of the ''Complete Peerage'' make no mention of her.
2 CONT >'''4.''' Unless a primary source is found to prove Agatha's parentage, her present parental linkage remains an insupportable presumption. — (Ken Shelley, 30 Aug 2022)
2 CONT >'''<nowiki>---------------------------------------------------</nowiki>'''
2 CONT '''Agatha de Ferrers'''   Mistress of John I Lackland, King of England & possible mother of his illegitimate daughter Joan, who married Llewellyn "the Great"; Prince of Wales
2 CONT '''Born''' ca.1167/72  Chartley, Stafforshire, England; d.19 Oct 1216 Aberconway, Caernarvonshire, Wales 
2 CONT ''Assumed'' '''Father''' William de Ferrers, 3rd Earl Derby1 b. c 1136, d. b 21 Oct 1190  
2 CONT ''Assumed'' '''Mother''' Sibyl de Braose b. c 1150, d. a 5 Feb 1228 
2 CONT
2 CONT Child # 6 of 12
2 CONT
2 CONT >1.   William de Ferrers  b.abt.1162 
2 CONT >2.   Ermintrude Ferrers  b.abt.1163 
2 CONT >3.   Margery Ferrers  b.abt.1165 
2 CONT >4.   Elizabeth de Ferrers  b.abt.1166 
2 CONT >5.   Hugh de Ferrieres  b.abt.1167 d.1204 
2 CONT >6.   '''Agatha de Ferrers'''  b.abt.1168
2 CONT >7.   Son de Ferrers  b.ca.1168 
2 CONT >8.   Millicent de Ferrers  b.abt.1170 
2 CONT >9.   Son de Ferrers  b.ca.1170 
2 CONT >10.  Son de Ferrers  b.ca.1172
2 CONT >11.  Isabel de Ferrieres  b.abt.1172 d.bef.May 31, 1252;  bur.St. John Hospital Chruch, Lechlade, Gloucestershire, England;  m. (1) abt. 1190 Roger de Mortimer;  m. (2) abt. 1215 Piers FitzHerbert 
2 CONT >12.  Robert Ferrers  b.abt.1177 d.1227 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Family 1''':  Mistress of John I Lackland, King of England, Duke of Normandy, Count of Anjou (b. 24 Dec 1166, d. 19 Oct 1216) was the son of Henry II, King of England, 11th Count of Anjou, Duke of Normandy, Count of Maine & Aqu
2 CONC itaine and Eleanor of Aquitaine.
2 CONT
2 CONT Agatha Ferrers (concubine of John "Lackland, King of England)  She did not marry John Lackland, King of England, Duke of Normandy, Count of Anjou. They had an affair when they both were young.  
2 CONT
2 CONT Notes:  It is known that Agatha was a mistress of John, but it is only supposition that she is the mother of his child, Joan. Others suggest that Joan's mother was Clemence, the wife of Henry Pinel.
2 CONT
2 CONT ====Comments====
2 CONT
2 CONT http://freepages.genealogy.rootsweb.com/~havens5/p23509.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT Quote from a discussion of the Joan of England on Soc.Medieval-L.  The identity of Joan's mother is unknown. Agatha Ferrers is a nice guess, but is unsupported by contemporary evidence. The only time Joan's mother is mentioned by 
2 CONC name is in the Tewkesbury Annals, where she is called "Queen Clementia". Is this a different name for Agatha Ferrers? Possibly, but not likely.
2 CONT
2 CONT Should you take "Agatha Ferrers" out of your charts? Probably. What I would do is replace her with "Clementia, otherwise unidentified", and include a large footnote with all of the speculative identities for her, including Agatha 
2 CONC Ferrers. Doug Richardson, taking "Clementia" as a name and not an epithet, has come up with some plausible, but not conclusive, evidence of who she might be (see other recent threads in this group). 
2 CONT
2 CONT ===============
2 CONT
2 CONT Child #1: Joan of North Wales or Joanna Plantagenet of England (b. circa 1188 London, Middlesex, England;  d. 30 Mar 1237 at:  Abner, Carnarvonshire, Wales) was born illegitimately. She is the daughter of John I 'Lackland', King o
2 CONC f England  and Agatha de Ferrers .
2 CONT
2 CONT Married: 18 Jun 1205, England; Llewelyn Fawr (Prince) of Gwynedd (Llywelyn "the Great"; Prince of Wales; Llywelyn ap Iorwerth (ap Jorweth) of North Wales (b. ca. 1173 Aberffraw Castle, Anglsy, North Wales; d. 11 Apr 1240, Aberconw
2 CONC ay, Carnarvonshire, Wales) 
2 CONT
2 CONT >Children:  (grandchildren of Agatha)
2 CONT >1. Elen (Helen, Helena) verch Llywelyn; 
2 CONT >2. Angharad verch Llywelyn;  
2 CONT >3.  Dafydd ap Llywelyn 
2 CONT >>Possible Other Children:  
2 CONT >>4.  Llewelyn (Prince) of North Wales
2 CONT >>5.  Gwladys Dhu "Dark eyed" verch Llewelyn
2 CONT >>6.  Margaret of Wales    
2 CONT
2 CONT ====Citations====
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. Some Early English Pedigrees, by Vernon M. Norr, p. 68;  
2 CONT
