1 NOTE {geni:about_me} =William II de Beauchamp=
2 CONT * Born about 1130 [uncertain] in Worcestershire, England  
2 CONT * Died about 1197 [uncertain] at about age 67 in Worcestershire, England
2 CONT * Son of William de Beauchamp and Maud Braose
2 CONT ----
2 CONT Some secondary sources have indicated [https://www.geni.com/people/Jeanne-de-Waleries/6000000000437613151 Joan de Walerie/Valery] was a daughter of a Thomas de Valerie and that she married William Beauchamp (d.  1197) but a thread
2 CONC  on SGM [soc.genealogy.medieval] suggests otherwise.
2 CONT ----
2 CONT William DE BEAUCHAMP  https://www.myheritage.com/research/record-14100-2312796716/william-de-beauchamp-in-filae-family-trees?indId=externalindividual-0b2452a30766ce3e914dc778380cf077&mrid=455dbe53af877f400947620db7dd0333&tr_id=m_v
2 CONC c4s5ol6kt_gear0xxtxd
2 CONT ===[http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/enguntac.htm#WilliamBeauchampdied1170  '''From Medlands:''']
2 CONT UNTITLED ENGLISH NOBILITY A - C
2 CONT v5.0 Updated 13 August 2025
2 CONT B.      BEAUCHAMP of ELMLEY, WORCESTERSHIRE
2 CONT
2 CONT '''WILLIAM [II] de Beauchamp''', son of WILLIAM [I] de Beauchamp & his wife Bertha de Briouse (-1197).  The primary source which confirms his parentage has not yet been identified.   The Red Book of the Exchequer, listing scutage 
2 CONC payments in [1190/91], records "Willelmus de Bello Campo" paying "lxx s de militibus, quos tenet de Rege in diversis comitatius, vii milites" in Worcestershire[927].  The Red Book of the Exchequer, listing scutage payments in [119
2 CONC 4/95], records "Willelmo de Bello Campo" paying "vii l de toto sentagio quod promisit domino Regi" in Worcestershire[928].  The Annals of Worcester record the death in 1197 of “Willelmus de Bello Campo”[929]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT m AMICE, daughter of ---.  The primary source which confirms her marriage has not yet been identified.  The introduction to the Beauchamp Cartulary states that it is clear from the cartulary of Westwood priory that "Amice (or Avic
2 CONC e) ‘lady of Salwarpe’ was the mother of William [II]’s heir and other children"[930].  The Rotuli Curiæ Regis record a claim in 1198 by "Amic de Bello Campo" against "Will de Brause" relating to land in Oxfordshire[931]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT [Mistress (1): --- de Salwarpe, sister of Odo de Salwarpe, daughter of ---.  The identity of the mother of Juliana, daughter of William [II] de Beauchamp, is suggested by the three charters quoted below.  The implication of the do
2 CONC cuments is that Juliana was illegitimate, and that the grant of property made by William [II] de Beauchamp to Odo de Salwarpe under the first document amounted to compensation for getting his sister pregnant, on the understanding 
2 CONC that the property in question would later be transmitted to his [illegitimate] daughter, the transfer being effected by the second document and confirmed by the third.  However, see the reference under Amice, wife of William [II] 
2 CONC de Beauchamp, to her being “lady of Salwarpe” which, if correct, suggests that this possible mistress may have been the same person as his wife.]
2 CONT
2 CONT William [II] & his wife had two children: 
2 CONT
2 CONT 1.         WILLIAM [III] de Beauchamp
2 CONT
2 CONT 2.         WALTER [III] de Beauchamp 
2 CONT
2 CONT William [II] had one [probably illegitimate] child by [Mistress (1)]: 
2 CONT
2 CONT 3.          JULIANA .  "Willelmus de Bello Campo" granted land previously held by "magister Alvricus cocus" to "Odoni de Salewarp fideli meo" by charter dated to [1170/97][985].  "Odo de Salewarp" granted "totam terram meam de Sto
2 CONC lton" to "Juliane [nepote/nepte] mee filie Willelmi de Bello Campo" by charter dated to [1170/97][986].  "Odo de Salewarp" confirmed "totam terram…in villa de Stoltoni que fuit Alvrici coci cum terra de Sudwode" to "Juliane filie 
2 CONC Willelmi de Bello Campo et [nepos/nepte] mee" by charter dated to [1170/97][987]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ===References 
2 CONT #[http://thepeerage.com/p39778.htm#i397779 William de Beauchamp] thepeerage.com
2 CONT ## [S1916] Tim Boyle, "re: Boyle Family," e-mail message to Darryl Roger Lundy, 16 September 2006. Hereinafter cited as "re: Boyle Family
2 CONT # WikiTree contributors, "William (Beauchamp) de Beauchamp (abt.1130-abt.1197)," WikiTree: The Free Family Tree, (https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Beauchamp-440 : accessed 30 August 2025). 
2 CONT # See MedLands [http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/ENGLISHNOBILITYMEDIEVAL3.htm#BeauchampMMatildaLimesey --- de Beauchamp].
2 CONT # Avicia, wife of William de Beauchamp (d. 1170). Thread of 2010. Soc. Gen. Medieval SGM. < [https://groups.google.com/g/soc.genealogy.medieval/c/g-Z_12VnIxw/m/he99cK5sBAAJ link] > 
2 CONT # Braose Beauchamp Marriage. Thread of 2017. Soc. Gen. Medieval SGM. < [https://groups.google.com/g/soc.genealogy.medieval/c/ZSgXNf442uk/m/ImLzzaLPCAAJ link] > 
2 CONT # Grazebrook, H. Sydney (Henry Sydney), 1836-1896. ''The heraldry of Worcestershire : …'' (1873). Page 37-38.  “Beauchamp, of Elmley Castle.” < [https://archive.org/details/heraldryworcest00grazgoog/page/n96/mode/2up Archive.Org] 
2 CONC > 
