1 NOTE {geni:about_me} "Matilda Beauchamp married Robert IV Marmion, 6th Baron Tamworth, son of Robert Marmion, 5th Lord Scrivelsby and Elizabeth of Rethel. Matilda Beauchamp died after 1181." — ''The Complete Peerage'', Cokayne, Vol. VI
2 CONC II, p. 507, 509; Wallop Family, p. 528. https://our-royal-titled-noble-and-commoner-ancestors.com/p763.htm#i22902
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Family and descendants
2 CONT Marmion first married Matilda/Maud, daughter of William de Beauchamp of Elmley, with whom he had the following issue:
2 CONT
2 CONT Robert the Elder (d.1241), of Tamworth, Scrivelsby and Normandy.
2 CONT Mabel m. Hugh de Say of Richard's Castle
2 CONT daughter m. William de Lizures
2 CONT and secondly, to Philippa, who bore him:
2 CONT
2 CONT Robert the Younger, of Winteringham, Coningsby and Tanfield.
2 CONT William, of Torrington and Normandy.
2 CONT Palmer claimed that he had at least the following three additional sons:
2 CONT
2 CONT Geoffrey,
2 CONT Phllip (d. 1276)
2 CONT Manasser (aka Manser or Mauncer)
2 CONT
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Robert_Marmion,_3rd_Baron_Marmion_of_Tamworth
