1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 
2 CONT MATTHEW FitzHerbert (-[13 Jun 1230/Feb 1231]). m (before Jun 1200) JOAN Patric, daughter of --- & his wife Mabel Patric[619] (-after 21 Feb 1231). Matthew & his wife had three children:
2 CONT
2 CONT a) HERBERT FitzMatthew (-3 or 5 Feb 1245). "Herbert son of Matthew" was granted "the manor of Warblinton, late of Robert de Curcy" dated 10 Jun 1231[621]. "Herbert son of Matthew" was granted "a weekly market…at Emeleswurth…" date
2 CONC d 20 Apr 1239[622]. m MILLICENT Paynell, daughter of WILLIAM Paynell of Bampton, Devon & his wife Alice Briwere (-before 1249). The Complete Peerage states that Herbert FitzMatthew married “Milicent da. and coh. of William Paynel 
2 CONC of Bampton, Devon” but does not cite the corresponding primary source[623]. An indication of the connection between the two families is provided by the order dated 4 Feb 1228 under which Henry III King of England granted "custodia
2 CONC m terre et heredis Willelmi Paynel" to "Hereberto filio Mathey" and ordered the sheriff of Devon to release them to him[624]. She must have died childless before 1249 when an inquisitions after her brother’s death name his sister 
2 CONC Aude as his heir.
2 CONT
