2 CONT
2 CONT Henry de Bohun, 1st Earl of Hereford From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia Jump to: navigation, search
2 CONT
2 CONT Henry de Bohun, 1st Earl of Hereford (1176 – 1220) was an English Norman nobleman.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was Earl of Hereford and Hereditary Constable of England from 1199 to 1220.
2 CONT
2 CONT Lineage
2 CONT
2 CONT He was the son of Humphrey de Bohun and Margaret of Huntingdon, Princess of Scotland, daughter of Henry of Scotland, 3rd Earl of Huntingdon, a son of David I of Scotland. His paternal grandmother was Margaret, daughter of Miles de
2 CONC  Gloucester, 1st Earl of Hereford and Constable of England. Bohun's half-sister was Constance, Duchess of Brittany.
2 CONT
2 CONT Earldom
2 CONT
2 CONT The male line of Miles of Gloucester having failed, on the accession of King John of England, Bohun was created Earl of Hereford and Constable of England (1199).
2 CONT
2 CONT Henry de Bohun was one of the 25 sureties of the Magna Carta in 1215, and was subsequently excommunicated by the Pope.
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage & children
2 CONT
2 CONT He married Maud de Mandeville of Essex, daughter of Geoffrey Fitzpeter, 1st Earl of Essex. Their children were:
2 CONT
2 CONT    1. Humphrey de Bohun, 2nd Earl of Hereford
2 CONT    2. Maud de Bohun, married Henry d'Oilly of Hook Norton, Oxfordshire.
2 CONT    3. Ralph de Bohun of Hereford, was father to Sir Franco de Bohun of Midhurst who married Sybil de Ferrers, daughter of William de Ferrers, 5th Earl of Derby. Ralph and Sybil are ancestors to the famous Daniel Boone in a direct 
2 CONC unbroken male-line.
2 CONT
2 CONT Later career
2 CONT
2 CONT He was also a supporter of King Louis VIII of France and was captured at the Battle of Lincoln in 1217.
2 CONT
2 CONT He died whilst on pilgrimage to the Holy Land. He was succeeded by his son Humphrey de Bohun, 2nd Earl of Hereford in 1220. Preceded by Humphrey de Bohun 	Lord High Constable 1199–1220 	Succeeded by The Earl of Hereford Preceded b
2 CONC y New Creation 	Earl of Hereford 1199–1220 	Succeeded by Humphrey de Bohun
2 CONT
2 CONT References
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Ancestral Roots of Certain American Colonists Who Came to America Before 1700 by Frederick Lewis Weis; Line 84-26
2 CONT     * Cokayne, G. (ed. by V. Gibbs). Complete Peerage of England, Scotland, Ireland, Great Britain and the United Kingdom. London:1887-1896, H-457-459
2 CONT
2 CONT http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Henry_de_Bohun,_1st_Earl_of_Hereford
