2 CONT     (4) Henry de Bohun:  (b.1176, d.June 1, 1220, buried Llanthony Abbey in
2 CONT     Gloucester).  He married Maud Fitz Piers, daughter of Geoffrey Fitz Piers, Earl
2 CONT     of Essex (d.1212 and his wife Beatrix de Sayle.  Henry was the first Earl of
2 CONT     Hereford and constable of England through the hereditary right to the office
2 CONT     from his great grandfather Miles of Gloucester.  On the accession of King John
2 CONT     I he was created Earl of Hereford in 1199.  In 1200 he was sent with other
2 CONT     nobles to summon his uncle, William the Lion of Scotland to appear at Lincoln
2 CONT     to do homage to King John of England.  In 1215 he joined the barons who
2 CONT     obtained the concessions of the Magna Charta and was one of the twenty-five
2 CONT     barons appointed to insure its observance.  On John's death he still adheredto
2 CONT     the party who wanted to make Louis of France King of England and was taken
2 CONT     prisoner at the battle of Lincoln in 1217.  He died on a pilgrimage to the Holy
2 CONT     Land and was succeeded by his son Humphrey.--Adec,FHL 929.273,C769w
