1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ====Concern
2 CONT * '''Stirnet's "Egerton01"''' page (link below) indicates that this William and Beatrix Monhalt (de Montalt) were extramarital paramours, but Stirnet's "MZmisc07" page indicates that they married.  Further research is warranted.
2 CONT
2 CONT ====Brief Biography and Family
2 CONT * had other issue by Margery de Linton besides who is shown here; Stirnet's "Egerton01" page (link below) shows Roger as his son by Margery de Linton instead of by Beatrix Monhalt (de Montalt)
2 CONT
2 CONT ====Link
2 CONT * https://stirnet.com/genie/data/british/ee/egerton01.php#top (membership required in order to view without interruption)
2 CONT
2 CONT ====Content for Clean-up
2 CONT Please see Darrell Wolcott: The "Malpas" Family in Cheshire; http://www.ancientwalesstudies.org/id152.html. (Steven Ferry, April 19, 2020.)
2 CONT
2 CONT William ap David ap William ap David ap William II ap Sir William, was born about 1180. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He was the partner of Beatrix, daughter of Robert de Montalt, seneschal to the Earl of Chester.
2 CONT
2 CONT Their son was David was born about 1210; he was not http://www.geni.com/people/Sir-David-le-Clerk-de-Malpas-Justice-of-Chester/6000000004868907755?through=6000000000538172995
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT From http://cybergata.com/roots/1826.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT ~The Visitation of Cheshire in the Year 1580, pgs. 163-162, shows David de Mallpas, son of David, son of Rogerus Malpas, son of '''William de Malpas and Margeria daughter of Cadogan de Linton''', son of Dan David, and lastly, son 
2 CONC 0f Willielmus Belward & Margreta Keveliock.
2 CONT
2 CONT • Background Information. 713 
2 CONT
2 CONT Sir William de Malpas, was the son and heir of David de Malpas, or David le Clerc and his wife Catherine, daughter of Owain Vaghan, lord of Meilor. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He left no legitimate issue with his wife, Margaret, daughter of Cadogan de Lynton, but he did with his mistress, Beatrix Montalt, the daughter the Seneschal of the earl of Chester. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Their children were:
2 CONT
2 CONT * Sir David de Malpas, "the Bastard," a.k.a. Sir David le Clerc, who became the heir to his father's moiety of Malpas. David married Constance, the daughter of Owain de Kevelioc, prince of Powys.
2 CONT * Roger de Malpas, ancestor of the Malpas of Hampton.
2 CONT * NINE daughters, which are not mentioned by Ormerod on the Malpas pedigree.
2 CONT
2 CONT ~George Ormerod's ''The History of County Palatine and City of Chester'', Vol II, p. 598
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ====Notes
2 CONT * From [http://www.ancientwalesstudies.org/id152.html THE "MALPAS" FAMILY IN CHESHIRE] By Darrell Wolcott * c. William ap David ap William ap David ap William II ap Sir William, born c. 1180, married Beatrix, daughter of Robert de
2 CONC  Montalt, seneschal to the Earl of Chester.
2 CONT * [http://www.ancientwalesstudies.org/sitebuildercontent/sitebuilderpictures/.pond/malpaspedigreex.jpg.w560h549.jpg 1.  Visitation of Cheshire, 1580]
2 CONT * David (4) who married Margaret (5) was not "le clerk" but the son of William II and father of William born c. 1120 whose son David of c. 1150 was the father of William (6) who married Beatrix (7).  They had a son David (8) who w
2 CONC as the father of Beatrix (10).  
2 CONT * [http://www.ancientwalesstudies.org/sitebuildercontent/sitebuilderpictures/malpaspedigreeo.jpg 2.  Pedigree from Ormerod's History of Cheshire, vol 2, 598:]
2 CONT * Neither David in this pedigree is the man called "le Clerk".  The man at the top is David of c. 1150 ap William ap David ap William II ap Sir William. 
2 CONT * The first William in the chart was born c. 1180 and did marry Beatrix, daughter of Robert de Montalt.  This Robert de Montalt was descended from the family of seneschals who served the Earls of Chester, being born c. 1160 and th
2 CONC e son of the elder Robert de Montalt, the latter being a son of Ralph fitz Norman.
2 CONT * Their son David was neither "le clerk" nor "the Bastard", both of those being earlier men named David in the Malpas family.  Since his daughter Beatrix is known to have inherited one-fourth of Malpas, we may safely assume her fa
2 CONC ther was a legitimate heir of his father.
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Sir William de MALPAS Knight (son of Sir David de MALPAS Knight & Catherine Vaughan) 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7 was born 1182 in Malpas, Cheshire, England. He married 8 Beatrix de MOHAUT.
2 CONT
2 CONT Beatrix de MOHAUT (daughter of  Robert de MOHAUT) 1, 2, 3, 4 was born 1182 in Chester, Cheshire, England. She married 5 Sir William de MALPAS Knight.
2 CONT
2 CONT They had the following children:
2 CONT *  M	i	 Sir David de MALPAS Knight was born 1200 and died 1260.
2 CONT *  M	ii	 Roger de MALPAS was born 1210.
2 CONT
2 CONT Other marriages:  LYNTON, Margaret de.  Margaret de LYNTON 1, 2 was born 1200 in West Lynton, East Riding, Yorkshire, England. She married Sir William de MALPAS Knight on 1221 in Malpas, Cheshire, England.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT * [http://freepages.genealogy.rootsweb.com/~hwbradley/aqwg1502.htm#25169 Hal Bradley's Rootsweb database]
2 CONT ** 1. Ormerod, George, The History of the County Palatine and City of Chester (London: Lackington, Hughes, Mavor & Jones, 1819.), 2:598, Family History Library, 942.71 H2or.
2 CONT ** 2. Ormerod, G., History of the County Palatine of Chester, 2:641.
2 CONT ** 3. Ormerod, G., History of the County Palatine of Chester, 2:628.
2 CONT ** 4. Glover, Robert, The Visitation of Cheshire in the Year 1580 (London: 1882.), p. 182, Los Angeles Public Library, Gen 942.005 H284 v.18.
2 CONT ** 5. Collections for a History of Staffordshire (Birmingham: William Salt Archaeological Society, 1888.), 9 (2): 50, Family History Library, 942.46 B4sc.
2 CONT ** 6. Boyer, Carl, Medieval Welsh Ancestors of Certain Americans (Santa Clarita, California: C. Boyer, 2004.), p. 18, Family History Library, 942.9 D2bc.
2 CONT ** 7. Wrottesley, George, Pedigrees from the Plea Rolls (London: Harrison, 1905. FHL BRITISH Film #990,070 Item 1.), p. 137, Family History Library.
2 CONT ** 8. Ormerod, G., History of the County Palatine of Chester, 2:598.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Married to Beatrix de Mohaut (http://www.ancientwalesstudies.org/id152.html)
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ~The Visitation of Cheshire in the Year 1580, pgs. 163-162, shows David de Mallpas, son of David, son of Rogerus Malpas, son of William de Malpas and Margeria daughter of Cadogan de Linton, son of Dan David, and lastly, son 0f Wil
2 CONC lielmus Belward & Margreta Keveliock.
2 CONT
2 CONT ~George Ormerod's The History of County Palatine and City of Chester, Vol II, pg. 628, Sir William de Malpas, Knt., son and heir of the barony of Malpas. 527,713
2 CONT
2 CONT bullet  Noted events in his life were:
2 CONT
2 CONT • Background Information. 713  • Sir William de Malpas, was the son and heir of David de Malpas, or David le Clerc and his wife Catherine, daughter of Owain Vaghan, lord of Meilor. He left no legitimate issue with his wife, Margar
2 CONC et, daughter of Cadogan de Lynton, but he did with his mistress, Beatrix Montalt, the daughter the Seneschal of the earl of Chester. Their children were:
2 CONT
2 CONT • Sir David de Malpas, "the Bastard," a.k.a. Sir David le Clerc, who became the heir to his father's moiety of Malpas. David married Constance, the daughter of Owain de Kevelioc, prince of Powys. • Roger de Malpas, ancestor of the
2 CONC  Malpas of Hampton. • NINE daughters, which are not mentioned by Ormerod on the Malpas pedigree.
2 CONT
2 CONT ~George Ormerod's The History of County Palatine and City of Chester, Vol II, p. 598
2 CONT
2 CONT William had a relationship with Beatrix de Montalt, daughter of Roger de Montalt and Unknown.713 (Beatrix de Montalt died after 1245 in Cheshire, England 713.)
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ===References 
2 CONT #http://www.ancientwalesstudies.org/id152.html William of c. 1120 had a son David (the man at the top of Ormerod's chart) who had sons '''William''' and and '''Phillip Goch''', between whom his 1/2 of Malpas was divided.  Thus all
2 CONC  the generations (after David at the top) in Ormerod's chart held 1/4 of Malpas.  The line "daughtered-out" with Beatrix; her 1/4 of Malpas went to her daughter Isabella, thence to that lady's son by Richard de Sutton.
