2 CONC s Nympton, Devon, which was granted to him by Roger his father in 1237/38 and was held by his grandson and representative Hugh Lord Mortimer…at his death in 1304"[1098].  m ROBERT de Mortimer of Richard’s Castle, Herefordshire, so
