2 CONT Citations
2 CONT
2 CONT [S37] Charles Mosley, editor, Burke's Peerage, Baronetage & Knightage, 107th edition, 3 volumes (Wilmington, Delaware, U.S.A.: Burke's Peerage (Genealogical Books) Ltd, 2003), volume 1, page 950. Hereinafter cited as Burke's Peera
2 CONC ge and Baronetage, 107th edition. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ------
2 CONT
2 CONT From [https://books.google.com/books?id=ZU59tRkdl2MC&lpg=PA479&ots=71H2hzspxn&dq=Sir%20Walter%20de%20Lindsay%2C%20of%20Ercildoun&pg=PA479#v=onepage&q=Sir%20Walter%20de%20Lindsay,%20of%20Ercildoun&f=false page 479] of Genealogical 
2 CONC and Heraldic Dictionary of the Peerage and Baronetage of the British Empire Bernard Burke Harrison and sons, 1865 - Baronetage - 1323 pages
2 CONT
2 CONT Malahule's great-grandson, Randolph De Toknt, who was extemporary with Richard 2ndj Duke of Normandy, had two sons, L Rooer, whose sons, Randolph and Robert, accompanied William the Conqueror to England in 1066, and were the ances
2 CONC tors of the houses of De Toeny and Stafford; li. Hcoo, who founded the family of De Lindsay. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He had two sons, Randolph De Lindsay, who accompanied William the Conqueror to England in 1006; Balderic De Lindsay, who, in 1036, held lands in Lincolnshire under Hugh Lupus, Earl of Chester. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Balderic de Lindsay was succeeded by his son,
2 CONT
2 CONT Walter De Lindsay, who was a great baron under David, Prince of Cumbria, afterwards King of Scotland, and was witness to the inquest of that prince into the possessions and rights of the see of Glasgow in 1110. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Walter de Lindsay was succeeded by his brother,
2 CONT
2 CONT William De Lindsay, who was Lord of Ercildoun. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He was succeeded by his son,
2 CONT
2 CONT Walter De Lindsay, of Ercildoun, who flourished about 1150. His son, ...
2 CONT ----
2 CONT '''He is a direct descendant of Charlemagne.'''
2 CONT This is his lineage:
2 CONT
2 CONT 1 Charlemagne
2 CONT 2 Louis I, The Pious
2 CONT 3 Charles II "the Bald", Western Emperor
2 CONT 4 Louis II the Stammerer, king of the West Franks
2 CONT 5 Ermentrude de France
2 CONT 6 Cunigunda, countess of Trèves & Ardennes
2 CONT 7 Siegfried I, count of Luxembourg
2 CONT 8 Frederick I, count of Moselgau
2 CONT 9 Gisèle de Luxemburg
2 CONT 10 Gislebert dit “Le Grand” de Gant (Gaunt), baron de Folkingham, seigneur de Hunmanby
2 CONT 11 Walter van Gent, lord of Folkingham (aka Walter de Lindsey)
2 CONT 12 Sir William de Lindsay
2 CONT ----
