1 NOTE He was witness to the charters of King David. The house of Lindsay owned very large estates in England and Scotland soon after the Norman conquest. Femily members had been conspicuous, not just for their wealth and power, but for 
2 CONC their important public service. The first Lindsay in Scotland was Walder de Lindissi, "noble knight," who accompanied David, Earl of Huntingdon to Cumbria early in the 12th century.
