2 CONT ===Origins 
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Walter_de_Gant Walter de Gant]  (died 1139), Lord of Folkingham was an English nobleman.
2 CONT
2 CONT Walter was a son of Gilbert de Gant and Alice, Dame de Montfort-sur-Risle. He inherited the English titles of his father, while his younger brother Hugh adopted his mother’s surname and arms to inherit her French titles and lands.
2 CONT He founded the priory at Bridlington, around 1113 for Augustinian Canons.[1] He died in 1139, while as a monk at Bardney Abbey and was buried there.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage and issue: 
2 CONT
2 CONT … '''Matilda de Gand''', married William de Welle.
2 CONT
