2 CONT '''William Fitz Walter, Lord of Welle; living circa 1166 and after 1184; married Rohese, daughter of Walter de Gant, Lord of Folkingham and Bridlington by his wife, Maud of Brittany, Lady of Swaledale''', and sister of Gilbert de 
2 CONC Gant II, Earl of Lincoln; from William and Rohese descend the de Welles family, summoned to Parliament as Barons from 1299, attainted 1474, created Viscount Welles in 1487 and extinct in 1498.
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.cracroft.org.uk/PEDVOL1.pdf
2 CONT
2 CONT =================================
2 CONT
2 CONT WELLES - Barons 
2 CONT WILLIAM, b ca 1155, tenant of SIMON de St. LIZ, Earl of Northampton for 6.5 knights’ fees, d bef 1198,''' m a sister of Gilbert de Gant, Earl of Lincoln, dau of WALTER de GANT''' (see under Gant for ancestors) by MAUD, dau of STEP
2 CONC HEN, Count of Brittany (see under Brittany for ancestors).
2 CONT * ROBERT de WELLE may have become Daptifer (steward) to Gilbert de Gant and thus have been father oh ROHESE who m SIMON de Kyme, ancestors of the Barons Kyme  
2 CONT * Solomon
2 CONT * Elizabeth, m Robert, son of Hugh de Tateschal
2 CONT
2 CONT http://members.pcug.org.au/~ronwells/710-9.htm
2 CONT
