1 NOTE EARLDOM OF LINCOLN (IV, 1)
2 CONT
2 CONT GILBERT DE GANT or GAUNT, son and heir of Walter DE GANT, byMaud, daughter of Stephen, COUNT OF BRITTANY, was born circa1120, at Bridlington, and baptized there. He fought on the sideof Stephen at the battle of Lincoln in February
2 CONC  1140/1, and wasthere taken prisoner by Ranulph II, Earl of Chester, whocompelled him to marry his niece. In 1147 he claimed the honourof Pontefract against Henry de Lacy, and in the fighting whichensued the priory of Pontefract w
2 CONC as burnt down, and Gilbert wasexcommunicated. Although William de Roumare had been createdEarl of Lincoln circa 1141, and presumably was still inenjoyment of that earldom, Gilbert was created by Stephen EARLOF LINCOLN circa 1147-4
2 CONC 8, and in about 1148, as Earl of Lincoln,founded Rufford Abbey, Notts.
2 CONT
2 CONT He married Rohese, sister of Gilbert and Roger, 1st & 2nd EARLSOF HERTFORD, and daughter of Richard FITZGILBERT of Clare, byAdeliz, daughter of Ranulph I, EARL OF CHESTER, and Lucy hiswife. He died s.p.m., in 1156, desiring to be 
2 CONC buried atBridlington Priory, where he had been baptised and brought upfrom childhood. His widow married Robert, Sewer of William dePercy. [Complete Peerage VII:672-3, XIV:436, (transcribed byDave Utzinger)]
