1 NOTE 6TH BARON MORTIMER OF WIGMORE; KNIGHTED BY THE KING 1253 AT WINCHESTER; SERVED ON THE MARCHES 1258-63, OPPOSING HIS COUSIN LLEWELLYN AP GRIFFITH; JOINED THE KING'S COUNCIL 4/1259; FOUGHT FOR THE KING AT LEWES 1264, BUT FLED THE FI
2 CONC ELD; DEVISED AND CARRIED OUT THE PLAN WHICH ENABLED THE IMPRISONED PRINCE EDWARD TO ESCAPE FROM HEREFORD CASTLE; COMMANDED THE REARGUARD AT EVESHAM 8/1265, AND AFTER MONTFORT'S DEATH, MONFORT'S HEAD WAS SENT TO MORTIMER'S LADY AT 
2 CONC WIGMORE AS A KEEPSAKE; RECEIVED HONOUR & LANDS OF OXFORD (FORFEITED BY ROBERT DE VERE), THOUGH TECHNICALLY NEVER HELD THE TITLE OF EARL OF OXFORD; BADLY DEFEATED AT BRECKNOCK BY THE WELSH (5/15/1266); TRUSTEE FOR PRINCE'S ESTATES 
2 CONC WHEN EDWARD WAS ON CRUSADE; SHERIFF OF SEVERAL COUNTIES; ROYAL JUSTICE; KING'S PRINCIPAL MILITARY COMMANDER IN WALES; WIDELY REGARDED BY HIS PEERS AS "THE MOST TRUSTWORTHY NOBLEMAN IN THE KINGDOM".
2 CONT
