2 CONT From Darrell Wolcott, Center for the Study of Ancient Wales, in discussing issues with the line in Dwnn ii, 127: "This goes way past my charts (I ended at Einion Sais) but my guess is that Dwnn meant "Dafydd ap Gruffudd Fychan ap 
2 CONC Gruffudd" and that 3 generations are omitted in the pedigree.  I suspect there is a repeating trio of Llewelyn ap Caswallon ap Hywel immediately following the men of those names who were "ap Owain Gwynedd".  And both men named Lle
2 CONC welyn ap Caswallon had a son named Gruffudd who named a son Gruffudd Fychan." This gives a stable timeline and would place Angharad ferch Gwilim at c. 1475/80, with her husband Llewelyn ap Heilyn at c. 1465. (Steven Ferry, July 13
2 CONC , 2020.)
2 CONT
2 CONT Please see Darrell Wolcott: The Children of Owain Gwynedd; http://www.ancientwalesstudies.org/id302.html (Steven Ferry, September 11, 2022.)
2 CONT
2 CONT Please see Darrell Wolcott: Hwfa ap Cynddelw, Lord of Llifon: http://www.ancientwalesstudies.org/id322.html (Steven Ferry, January 23, 2024.)
2 CONT
