0 @N6000000002187907008@ NOTE Pir of the Britons
1 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
1 CONT Jump to: navigation, search
1 CONT
1 CONT Pir was a legendary king of the Britons as accounted by Geoffrey of Monmouth. He was preceded by either Samuil or Penessil, and succeeded by Capoir.
1 CONT [edit]
1 CONT
1 CONT Sources
1 CONT
1 CONT In Historia Regum Britanniae, Geoffrey of Monmouth names Penessil as predecessor to Pir, with Samuil ruling before Penessil. Bill Cooper in his English translation of a contemporary Welsh chronicle on which Geoffrey supposedly bas
1 CONC ed his Historia, rather names Sawl benn Ychel as Pir's predecessor and comments that Geoffrey misinterpreted that name when latinizing it, thereby adding the intermediary king Penissel between Samuil and Pir. Aaron Thompson presen
1 CONC ts a similar succession in his English translation of the Historia by having a king Samuilpenissel preceding Pir.
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT Preceded by:
1 CONT Samuil
1 CONT or
1 CONT Penessil Mythical British Kings Succeeded by:
1 CONT Capoir
