0 @N6000000003051298290@ NOTE [Wikipedia, "Eiludd Powys", retrieved 22 Dec 07]
1 CONT Eiludd Powys was an early 7th century King of Powys.
1 CONT
1 CONT One theory asserts that when Manwgan ap Selyf came to the throne in 613 he was a young boy, which led to an invasion of Powys by Eluadd ap Glast (alias Eiludd Powys), the erstwhile King of Dogfeiling. The usurper probably managed 
1 CONC to hold the throne for some thirty years or more before he was killed fighting the Northumbrians, possibly at the Battle of Maes Cogwy (Oswestry) in 642. The Dogfeiling dynasty was finally crushed by the Saxons around 656.
