0 @N6000000001745130001@ NOTE CADWALADR (son of No. 9). He became King of Gwynedd after the death of his father.
1 CONT           "None of his deeds have been recorded, yet he must have been a figure of some distinction. He died
1 CONT           in the great plague of 664, and it is likely, notwithstanding his martial reputation, that he spent the close
1 CONT           of his life as a monk, for the church of Llangadwaladr in Anglesey claims him as its patron saint and
1 CONT           founder and churches were dedicated to him in other parts of Wales." (Lloyd.) It will be noted that
1 CONT           Prof. Lloyd has the date of his death 664. In The Annales Cambriae it is 682.
