0 @N6000000003949883540@ NOTE The existence of this king is dubious.  He is named among the forefears of Kenneth Macalpin, and was purportedly the son of Aed Find and the father of Alpin thru his marriage to Fergusa.  The start of his reign is set at 781and po
1 CONC ssibly he ruled only part of the kingdom, possibly only Kintyre.  He earned the nickanme of "the Poisonous" for his vicous tongue, rather than his murderous abilities.  However it is virtually impossible that he survived until 834
1 CONC  to pass the kingdom to his son Alpin.  However, he equates to the legendary Achaius who is attributed with establishing an accord with Charlemagne and with founding the original Noble Order of the Thistle.  (per Mike Ashley "The 
1 CONC Mammoth Book of British Kings & Queens", p206, #FC29c)
