0 @N6000000002187590890@ NOTE Aed of Dalriada
1 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.
1 CONT
1 CONT Aed of Dalriada the White (Scottish Gaelic: Aed Find or Aodh Airgneach) was king of Dál Riada from about 739 until 778. He was the son of Eochaid III of Dalriada, king of Dál Riada, and his wife, Spondan. He was married to Fergina
1 CONC , a possible daughter of Constantine, king of the Picts, and by her had Eochaid II.
1 CONT
1 CONT Aed defeated the Pictish king, Ciniod, in 768 at the Battle of Fortrui near Perth about 775.
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT House of Alpin
1 CONT Cadet Branch of the House of Uí Néill
1 CONT Born: Unknown; Died: 778 
1 CONT Preceded by:
1 CONT Eogan King of Dál Riada
1 CONT 739–778 Succeeded by:
1 CONT Fergus II 
0 @N6000000002315775465@ NOTE (Etfinus or Hugh the White), King of Scots 748-778 "748. Ed-fin (Hugh the White) son of Eochy-Rinnavel (Wry-nose) reigned 30 years 778. Ed-fun (White Hugh), King of Dalriada, in the same year in which Neill Frasch, king of ireland
1 CONC , died, came to his end." 
