0 @N6000000003949663686@ NOTE 4096. Gwriad, probably from the Isle of Man, and possibly the person named on an inscription ("CRUX GURIAT") on a cross in the Isle of Man which has been dated to the eighth or ninth century.  [Note:  The genealogy which purports 
1 CONC to make Gwriad a direct male-line descendant of Llywarch Hen is almost certainly a late fabrication.  It is more likely that his paternal ancestors were among those who are named in HG.4, but the exact line of descent (if any) is 
1 CONC uncertain, and Gwriad's parentage must be regarded as unknown.  See SW for a discussion of these issues.  See also GH.] 
