0 @N6000000003949663094@ NOTE Teuder began ruling about 730, as Rhain passed his sub-kingdom to Aust, a younger brother. At this time it was invaded by Seisyll, King of Ceredigion, who conquered Ystrad Towy, and Rhain's kingdom was split in two. Both areas bec
1 CONC ame known for a time as Rheinwg after their king (Rhain). It is not known when Teuder died, but his son ruled until 798. Teuder was king of only Dyfed.  King of Dyfed #EC15 in Mike Ashley's "Kings and Queens of England, p137
