0 @N6000000003949663050@ NOTE Sought help from King Alfred the Great and united with him against the Viking threat.   Ruled 885-893.  #EC20 (Ashley's Kings & Queens of England)
1 CONT Hyfaidd was the son of Princess Tangwystl of Dyfed by a lowborn Welshman named Bledrig. He was known as something of a tyrant who often plundered the Cathedral of Mynyw (St.Davids) and expelled the monks. However, Hyfaidd had his 
1 CONC own oppressor in the person of King Anarawd of Gwynedd and his brothers. In order to stop Anarawd's conquests at the Dyfed border, Hyfaidd submitted to the overlordship of King Alfred the Great of England in the 880s, as described
1 CONC  by Asser, the latter's biographer. He died in 893
