0 @N6000000002187763348@ NOTE Anarawd ap Rhodri
1 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.
1 CONT
1 CONT Anarawd ap Rhodri (died 916) was a King of Gwynedd.
1 CONT
1 CONT Anarawd's father Rhodri the Great had eventually become ruler of most of Wales, but on his death in 878 his kingdom was shared out between his sons, with Anarawd inheriting the throne of Gwynedd. Anarawd and his brothers Cadell an
1 CONC d Merfyn are recorded as cooperating closely against the rulers of the remaining lesser kingdoms of Wales. Earl Aethelred of Mercia invaded Gwynedd in 881, but Anarawd was able to defeat him with much slaughter in a battle at the 
1 CONC mouth of the River Conwy, hailed in the annals as "God's vengeance for Rhodri", Rhodri having been killed in battle against the Mercians.
1 CONT
1 CONT Anarawd now made an alliance with the Danish king of York in an attempt to guard himself against further Mercian attacks. When this alliance proved unsatisfactory, he came to an agreement with Alfred the Great of Wessex, visiting 
1 CONC Alfred at his court. In exchange for Alfred's protection Anarawd recognised the supremacy of Alfred. This was the first time a ruler of Gwynedd had accepted the supremacy of an English king, and formed the basis for the homage whi
1 CONC ch was demanded by the English crown from then on.
1 CONT
1 CONT In 894 Anarawd was able to repel a raid by a Danish host on North Wales, and the following year raided Ceredigion and Ystrad Tywi in southern Wales. He is reported as having some English troops under his command for these raids. I
1 CONC n 902 an attack on Anglesey by some of the Danes of Dublin under Ingimund was repulsed. Anarawd died in 916 and was succeeded by his son Idwal Foel (=Idwal the Bald).
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT [edit]
1 CONT References
1 CONT John Edward Lloyd (1911). A history of Wales: from the earliest times to the Edwardian conquest, Longmans, Green & Co.. 
1 CONT
1 CONT Preceded by:
1 CONT Rhodri the Great Prince of Gwynedd
1 CONT 878–916 Succeeded by:
1 CONT Idwal Foel ab Anarawd 
