0 @N6000000001744855241@ NOTE [s2.FTW]
1 CONT
1 CONT HYWEL DHA (son of No. 17). He and his brother Clydog became rulers of Ceredigion and
1 CONT           Ystrad Turgi which were united to form Seisyllwg. Clydog died in 920 and Hywel became sole ruler.
1 CONT           He was called Hywel Dha (Howell the Good) on account of the mild and beneficent character of his
1 CONT           reign. He married Elen, daughter of Llywarch ap Hyfaidd, King of Dyfed, and he took possession of
1 CONT           Dyfed after the death of her father. He annexed Kydweli and Gwyr without the use of force. He
1 CONT           expelled Iago and Ieuaf from Gwynedd and seized the kingdom.
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT           He acquired Powys later, which made him king of all Wales. During his entire reign of forty years or
1 CONT           more he lived at peace with the Anglo-Saxons and he had very little trouble with the neighboring petty
1 CONT           kingdoms. His success in uniting the Welsh people under one government would entitle him to
1 CONT           distinction, but his fame rests largely on the fact that he was the first great law-giver of the Welsh
1 CONT           people. He called a few of the wise and learned men as counsellors and a code of just laws was
1 CONT           formed which became the law of the land and the basis of all later Welsh jurisprudence. He made a
1 CONT           pilgrimage to Rome, accompanied by a number of Welsh princes and church dignitaries. It is said that
1 CONT           he went to Rome to submit his laws to the Pope for his approval. He died in 950 loved and revered
1 CONT           by his subjects.HYWEL DHA (son of No. 17). He and his brother Clydog became rulers of Ceredigion and
1 CONT           Ystrad Turgi which were united to form Seisyllwg. Clydog died in 920 and Hywel became sole ruler.
