0 @N6000000001355643333@ NOTE John Davies, A History of Wales, Allen Lane- The Penguin Press, London, 1993, states, "About 904, Llywarch ap Hyfaidd, king of Dyfed, died;his kingdom came into the posession of Hywel ap Cadell ap Rhodri, theruler of Seisyllwg and
1 CONC  the husband of Elen, Llywarch's sister. It would appear that Hywel also took possesion of Brycheiniog, for its royalline ends with Tewdwr ap Griffri, who died about 930. The enlarged kingdom came to be known as Deheubarth, a unit
1 CONC  of central importance in the history of Wales during the following four centuries. Deheubarth was united with the territories of Idwal ab Anarawd ap Rhodri -- Gwynedd and Powys -- in 942, and Hywel died in 950 the ruler of a king
