1 CONT Death
1 CONT Rhys was able to withstand the increasing Norman pressure following the end of William's reign in 1087 until 1093, when he was killed at Penrhys Rhondda by the Norman. He was engaged in the Battle of Hirwaun with the Normans at Hi
1 CONC rwaun Common near (Aberdare). Upon defeat he fled the battle site through forestry and up over the mountain to Penrhys where he was eventually caught and beheaded. // Events Donald III of Scotland comes to the throne of Scotland. 
1 CONC ... Rhondda Cynon Taff (Welsh: Rhondda Cynon Tâf) is a county borough in Glamorgan, South Wales. ... Norman conquests in red. ... 
