0 @N6000000003949726469@ NOTE Rhys claimed the kingdom of Deheubarth after the death of Rhys ap Owain, but he needed to prove himself against Caradog ap Gruffydd.  Caradog mustered his forces in 1081 and pressed Rhys back to the coast until Rhys was forced to 
1 CONC seek refuge in Dyfed.  Rhys combined forces with Gruffydd ap Cynan and they defeated and killed Caradog.  at the battle of Mynydd Carn.  William the Conqueror and Rhys met and agreed to a treaty allowing Rhys to rule if he kept th
1 CONC e peace and paid annual tribute of 40 pounds.   In 1088 he was attacked by Madog ap Bleddyn with such ferocity that he was forced to flee to Ireland.  He raised the help of a Danish fleet, returned and killed Madog.   In April 109
1 CONC 3 he was killed in a skirmish with the Normans at Aberhonddu.  Mike Ashley "Kings and Queens of England, p 337-338)
