0 @N6000000002187865104@ NOTE Hoel II, Duke of Brittany
1 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
1 CONT Jump to: navigation, search
1 CONT Hoel II of Cornwall (died 1084) was count of Cornouaille (from 1058 as Hoel V) and duke of Brittany, from 1066 to his death. He inherited Brittany from duke Conan II, brother of his wife, Havise of Brittany. Hoel started the Cornw
1 CONC all dynasty of Brittany, which ruled the duchy until 1156.
1 CONT
1 CONT See also: Dukes of Brittany family tree
1 CONT
1 CONT Preceded by:
1 CONT Conan II Duke of Brittany Succeeded by:
1 CONT Alan IV 
0 @N6000000002248119892@ NOTE Hoel was count of Cornouille, and jure uxoris Duke of Brittany 1066.
