0 @N6000000001220382546@ NOTE [2753682.ged]
1 CONT
1 CONT 1st wife of Llywelyn the Great; mother of Gruffudd. [A History of Wales, p. 139]
1 CONT
1 CONT FOSTER, MINOR, NEWLIN LINES - 23rd ggrandmother
1 CONT
1 CONT Mistress of Llewellyn ap Iorwerth; mother of Gladys Dhu. [Ancestral Roots, p. 29]
1 CONT
1 CONT Dau. of Llywarch Goch ap Iowerth and Tanglwyst ferch Llywarch; m.? Llewelyn ap Iorwerth and w as mother of Gwladys ferch Llewelyn. [GRS 3.03, Automated Archives, CD#100]
1 CONT
1 CONT The only child known to be from the Welsh mistress Tangwystl is Griffith.  Lately, Douglas Ri chardson claimed that Gwenllian was her daughter as well. That conclusion is based on a lette r from William Marshall to Henry III descr
1 CONC ibing her as sister to Griffith. Because she was no t described as Henry's niece, Richardson concludes that she is not Joan's daughter. Her husba nd was in rebellion to Henry III and was among the English siding with Llywelyn in h
1 CONC is rebell ion. [Ken <KHF333@aol.com, 7 Jun 2002][3210710.ged]
1 CONT
1 CONT Note: Data of Vern Orvel Curtis, 1934; and LDS ancestral File of Augusti ne H. Ayers lists her as the daughter of Ethelred "the Unready" King of En gland. My data differs and so does that of Brian Tompsett of the Universi ty of Hu
1 CONC ll.[440.ged]
1 CONT
