0 @N6000000001503850031@ NOTE Paul Mackenzie posted to
1 CONT soc.genealogy.medieval on 1 Feb 1997:
1 CONT Subject: Re: The Beauchamps (was Re: Maud de Braose):
1 CONT D.G. Elwes published a number of papers on the Braoses in which he
1 CONT discusses the main members of the family together with the doubtful
1 CONT members. . . He does mention another connection between the de Braose
1 CONT and Beauchamps.
1 CONT "William (de Braose d1212) is stated to have been taken prisoner by
1 CONT King John in France with Prince Arthur 1202-03 and that although he
1 CONT was released from confinement the king appears ever after to have
1 CONT regarded him with an eye of suspicion and jealousy. Moreover, I think a
1 CONT not unlikely cause of King John quarrelling with William (de Braose) may
1 CONT befound in Inq. p.m. 26 Edw 111, 2nd Nos 66, which quotes a trial taking
1 CONT place before the Justices of Common Pleas in Easter, 6 Edw 1 (1278)
1 CONT between William de Beauchamp, Earl of Warwick, Plaintiff and William
1 CONT de Breuse, Defendent concerning the descent of the Castle of Sweynsey
1 CONT and the land of Gower. William de Breuse states that the land ofGower
1 CONT was granted to his ancestor William de Breuse by King John by charter in
1 CONT the fourth year of his reign 1203 and that therefore he cannot answer
1 CONT without the king. The Earl, in answer, says that he can answer as to the
1 CONT castle of Sweynsey, which he claims is not mentioned in the charter; the
1 CONT Earl also says that the said Charter was made in Normandy in the time of
1 CONT the war between the king of France and King John, on account of William
1 CONT threatening to depart from him and return to England, the king being
1 CONT terrified by said war; and that seisin of the land of Gower was never
1 CONT delivered to William. Now this must have been before the murder of
1 CONT Prince Arthur (by John)....and possibly William de Braose was...bribed to
1 CONT silence (by) grant of the lands of Gower"
