1 CONC he resulting settlement he was forced to hand over Gruffydd. The unlucky prince was to spend his last three years as a prisoner at the Tower of London, where he fell to his death in an attempted escape in 1244 (depicted in a medie
1 CONC val manuscript at right). Despite his seemingly bad luck, Gruffydd's son Llywelyn , was later successful in reuniting much of Wales under his rule, earning unprecedented recognition as "Prince of Wales" from Henry III under the te
1 CONC rms of the Treaty of Montgomery in 1267.
