1 CONC the grounds of his illegitmacy.
0 @N6000000005599129988@ NOTE Morgan was appointed Provost of Beverley in 1201.  He was nominated a s Bishop of Durham in 1213.  He ultimately traveled to Rome, but hisel ection was quashed by the Pope.
0 @N6000000003658779966@ NOTE From Plantagenet Ancestry:
1 CONT
1 CONT MORGAN FITZ ROY, clerk.  He was appointed Provost of Beverley in 1201.  He was nominated as Bishop of Durham in 1213.  He travelled to Rome, but his election was quashed by the Pope.  He died at Fountains Abbey about 1217.
0 @N6000000001220382663@ NOTE [2753682.ged]
1 CONT
1 CONT m. William de Lacy. [GRS 3.03, Automated Archives, CD#100]
1 CONT
1 CONT Dau. of Llewelyn ap Iorworth; m. William de Lacy; d. 1281. ["Barons de Braose"
1 CONT <http://freespace.virgin.net/doug.thompson/BraoseWeb/stage.htm]
1 CONT
1 CONT The only child known to be from the Welsh mistress Tangwystl is Griffith.  Lately, Douglas Ri chardson claimed that Gwenllian was her daughter as well. That conclusion is based on a lette r from William Marshall to Henry III descr
1 CONC ibing her as sister to Griffith. Because she was no t described as Henry's niece, Richardson concludes that she is not Joan's daughter. Her husba nd was in rebellion to Henry III and was among the English siding with Llywelyn in h
1 CONC is rebell ion. [Ken <KHF333@aol.com, 7 Jun 2002]
