1 CONC 3 (1866–8) · G. A. Holmes, The estates of the higher nobility in fourteenth-century England (1957) · R. Frame, English lordship in Ireland, 1318–1361 (1982) · R. R. Davies, Lordship and society in the march of Wales, 1282–1400 (19
1 CONC 78) · Tout, Admin. hist., vol. 3 · J. C. Davies, The baronial opposition to Edward II (1918) · J. R. Maddicott, Thomas of Lancaster, 1307–1322: a study in the reign of Edward II (1970) · J. R. S. Phillips, Aymer de Valence, earl o
1 CONC f Pembroke, 1307–1324: baronial politics in the reign of Edward II (1972) · N. Fryde, The tyranny and fall of Edward II, 1321–1326 (1979) · GEC, Peerage · G. A. Holmes, ‘The rebellion of the earl of Lancaster, 1328–9’, BIHR, 28 (1
